{
  "raw": {
    "https://jobs.cofc.edu/postings/18741": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of English (film and digital media production)",
      "description": "College of Charleston Employment Site | Assistant Professor of English (film and digital media production) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Applicant Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Academic Jobs Student Jobs Contact Us Assistant Professor of English (film and digital media production) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details POSTING INFORMATION Internal Title Assistant Professor of English (film and digital media production) Position Type Tenure-track School/Area School of Humanities and Social Sciences Department English Position Description The Department of English at the College of Charleston is seeking a tenure-track Assistant Professor of English with an emphasis in film and digital media production to begin on August 16, 2027. Required qualifications include a Ph.D. or terminal degree in English, Film Studies, Composition & Rhetoric, or a related field; a promising, emerging record in research and media production; and the potential to provide meaningful service to the department, campus, and the broader Charleston community. The English department offers a B.A. in English with three concentrations—Creative Writing, Literature & Film, and Writing, Rhetoric, & Publication—as well as an MFA in Creative Writing and a B.A. track for future secondary English teachers. We also lead a thriving Film Studies minor. The standard teaching assignment is 9 credits (typically three courses per semester), and teaching duties cover all levels, including First-Year Writing courses, introductory and upper-level courses, and graduate courses that support the MFA program. Specific teaching assignments will include Film Studies courses such as “Film and Media Arts Production” and “Special Topics in Film,” as well as Writing, Rhetoric, & Publication courses such as “Writing for the Web” and “Rhetoric in a Digital Age.” Faculty are encouraged to develop new courses aligned both with their research interests and program needs; to collaborate with Film Studies and Writing, Rhetoric, & Publication faculty in ongoing curricular and interdisciplinary expansion; to participate in the periodic teaching of first-year writing, first-year experience courses, and Honors College colloquia; and to mentor undergraduate independent studies and Bachelor’s Essays. Founded in 1770 and located in the heart of historic Charleston, South Carolina, the College of Charleston is a public institution of 11,000 students with a commitment to excellence in teaching and research. Charleston is a thriving city with abundant culture. Our interdisciplinary Film Studies program partners with local events, including the College’s annual Student Film Festival, the Charleston Film Festival, and the Nuovo Cinema Italiano Film Festival. Undergraduates in Film Studies and Writing, Rhetoric, & Publication programs intern as videographers, content developers, editors, script writers, and marketing assistants at a variety of local and national organizations. Applicants should submit: (1) a cover letter; (2) a statement of teaching philosophy; (3) CV; and (4) unofficial graduate transcripts by December 1 to https://jobs.cofc.edu/postings/18653 Contact Department Chair Dr. Anton Vander Zee (vanderzeeal@cofc.edu) with questions about applying. Additional materials, including letters of reference, will be requested after the initial review, and preliminary interviews will be conducted by Zoom. Special Instructions to Applicants Posting Date 10/20/2026 Closing Date 12/02/2026 Open Until Filled? No Posting Number F2026016P EEO Statement The College of Charleston is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate against any individual or group on the basis of sex, gender (including gender identity and/or expression), pregnancy, race, religion, color, national origin, age, disability, military or veteran status, sexual orientation, genetic information, and other classifications protected by applicable federal, state, and local laws. For more information, please visit eop.cofc.edu . Quicklink for Posting https://jobs.cofc.edu/postings/18653 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Application Curriculum Vitae Teaching Philosophy Unofficial Graduate Transcripts Optional Documents Email: jobs@cofc.edu General Information: 843.953.5512 Mailing Address: 66 George St. Charleston, SC 29424 HR Office 160 Calhoun St. Lightsey Building B36 Charleston, SC 29424 Campus Maps ©2020 All Rights Reserved. Privacy Policy To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.cofc.edu/postings/18740": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Anthropology",
      "description": "College of Charleston Employment Site | Assistant Professor of Anthropology Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Applicant Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Academic Jobs Student Jobs Contact Us Assistant Professor of Anthropology Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details POSTING INFORMATION Internal Title Assistant Professor of Anthropology Position Type Tenure-track School/Area School of Humanities and Social Sciences Department Sociology and Anthropology Position Description The College of Charleston Department of Sociology and Anthropology invites applications for a tenure-track assistant professor position beginning August 16, 2027. We seek a broadly trained cultural anthropologist who demonstrates a strong commitment to undergraduate teaching in at a undergraduate institution. The successful candidate will teach three courses per semester (typically limited to two course preps), ranging from a four-field introductory course to upper-level anthropology courses. Preference will be given to those that specialize in Political and Legal Anthropology with the ability to contribute to the College of Charleston’s pre-law advising program. We seek candidates with an active, current research agenda. A Ph.D. in Anthropology is required by the time of appointment. We welcome applicants from all backgrounds and especially value the ability to teach and mentor undergraduate students with differing experiences, needs, and perspectives. Apply online at JOBS . COFC . EDU . Only electronic applications submitted via this website will be considered. Please include the following materials with your online application: Cover letter outlining candidate’s current research agenda and teaching experience Curriculum vitae Unofficial graduate transcripts (official transcripts will be required upon hiring) One sample manuscript One sample syllabus (upload under “Other Document”) Contact information for three references who may be asked to submit letters of recommendation online at the virtual interview stage in the selection process, at least one of whom should specifically address your teaching qualifications. Review of applications will begin on Tuesday, December 15. Position open until filled. Questions regarding the position can be directed to Dr. Allison Foley at foleya@cofc.edu. The College of Charleston , located in Charleston, SC, is a public institution of 11,000 students with a commitment to excellence in teaching and research. The Department of Sociology and Anthropology consists of 17 faculty (7 anthropologists and 10 sociologists) and has approximately 190 undergraduate majors ( SOCY 125, ANTH 65). Applicants may learn more about the department at https://charleston.edu/sociology-anthropology/index.php. Special Instructions to Applicants Posting Date 10/20/2026 Closing Date 12/15/2026 Open Until Filled? Yes Posting Number F2026019P EEO Statement The College of Charleston is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate against any individual or group on the basis of sex, gender (including gender identity and/or expression), pregnancy, race, religion, color, national origin, age, disability, military or veteran status, sexual orientation, genetic information, and other classifications protected by applicable federal, state, and local laws. For more information, please visit https://charleston.edu/equal-opportunity-programs/index.php . Quicklink for Posting https://jobs.cofc.edu/postings/18632 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Application Curriculum Vitae Unofficial Graduate Transcripts Sample Publication 1 Other Document Optional Documents Email: jobs@cofc.edu General Information: 843.953.5512 Mailing Address: 66 George St. Charleston, SC 29424 HR Office 160 Calhoun St. Lightsey Building B36 Charleston, SC 29424 Campus Maps ©2020 All Rights Reserved. Privacy Policy To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
