    "https://jobs.cofc.edu/postings/18739": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Sociology",
      "description": "College of Charleston Employment Site | Assistant Professor of Sociology Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Applicant Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Academic Jobs Student Jobs Contact Us Assistant Professor of Sociology Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details POSTING INFORMATION Internal Title Assistant Professor of Sociology Position Type Tenure-track School/Area School of Humanities and Social Sciences Department Sociology and Anthropology Position Description The College of Charleston Department of Sociology and Anthropology invites applications for a tenure-track position at the Assistant Professor level beginning on August 16, 2027. Successful candidates will have earned a Ph.D. in Sociology, or closely related applied field, by the time of the appointment. We seek a broadly trained sociologist with specialization – and ability to teach courses – in the sociology of mental health, child and family welfare, or social work. The ideal candidate will have a strong commitment to teaching within an undergraduate institution and will be expected to teach a combination of courses in their area of specialization as well as introductory sociology courses and core sociology courses. Candidates should demonstrate evidence of ongoing scholarship. The College of Charleston , located in Charleston, SC, is a public institution of 11,000 students with a commitment to excellence in teaching and research. The Department of Sociology and Anthropology consists of 17 faculty (7 Anthropologists and 10 Sociologists) and has approximately 190 undergraduate majors ( SOCY 125, ANTH 65). Applicants may learn more about the department at https://charleston.edu/sociology-anthropology/index.php. Apply online at JOBS . COFC . EDU . Only electronic applications submitted via this website will be considered. Please include the following materials with your online application: Cover letter CV Unofficial graduate transcripts One sample manuscript One sample syllabus (load to “other documents”) Contact information for three references, who will be contacted at the virtual interview stage of the selection process Review of applications will begin on Monday, December 7, 2026. Position open until filled. Questions regarding the position can be directed to Heath Hoffmann at hoffmannh@cofc.edu. Special Instructions to Applicants Posting Date 10/20/2026 Closing Date 12/07/2026 Open Until Filled? Yes Posting Number F2026018P EEO Statement The College of Charleston is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate against any individual or group on the basis of sex, gender (including gender identity and/or expression), pregnancy, race, religion, color, national origin, age, disability, military or veteran status, sexual orientation, genetic information, and other classifications protected by applicable federal, state, and local laws. For more information, please visit https://charleston.edu/equal-opportunity-programs/index.php . Quicklink for Posting https://jobs.cofc.edu/postings/18631 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Application Curriculum Vitae Unofficial Graduate Transcripts Sample Publication 1 Other Document Optional Documents Email: jobs@cofc.edu General Information: 843.953.5512 Mailing Address: 66 George St. Charleston, SC 29424 HR Office 160 Calhoun St. Lightsey Building B36 Charleston, SC 29424 Campus Maps ©2020 All Rights Reserved. Privacy Policy To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
