    "https://jobs.cofc.edu/postings/18724": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructor of Marketing",
      "description": "College of Charleston Employment Site | Adjunct Instructor of Marketing Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Applicant Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Academic Jobs Student Jobs Contact Us Adjunct Instructor of Marketing Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Formal applications for the position must be submitted through the College’s PeopleAdmin™ site at http://jobs.cofc.edu . Submit online (1) a letter of application, (2) a recent CV, (3) unofficial graduate transcripts (official transcripts will be required for hiring), (4) a one-page statement of your teaching philosophy, (5) names and contact information of three references and (6) optional teaching evaluations if available. The department will begin considering applications when an adjunct opportunity becomes available and will continue considering applicants until the position is filled. Please contact the Search Chair with questions. Posting Details General Information Rank Adjunct Instructor of Marketing FLSA Exempt Position Type Adjunct Internal Title Adjunct Instructor of Marketing Department Marketing And International Business School/Area School of Business Posting Number A2026031P Specialty and subspecialty, if any, sought Marketing and related areas Courses to be covered Basic and/or upper-level Marketing courses as qualifications and demand warrant. Position Description POSITION : The Department of Marketing and International Business seeks qualified applicants for a marketing adjunct instructor starting January 2027. Adjunct assignments are temporary, may be full-time or part-time, and/or immediate or as needed. This job posting is not for a specific assignment or for a full-time faculty position, but rather for a pool of candidates who may be considered for teaching in Fall and Spring semesters. The successful candidate will teach undergraduate basic and/or upper-level marketing courses. Teaching responsibilities may include courses offered through the department’s undergraduate and graduate programs. Adjunct faculty pay scale: $3,420 for 3 credit hours, $6,820 for 6 credit hours, $11,556 for 9 credit hours QUALIFICATIONS : An M.A. or M.S. degree in marketing or a related field from an AACSB - or EQUIS -accredited program is the minimum academic requirement for this position. Candidates with significant industry or professional experiences in the marketing field are preferred. Candidates should demonstrate relevant academic and/or professional expertise and a commitment to high-quality teaching. Ideal applicants will also have college-level teaching experiences in basic and upper-level marketing courses at an AACSB -accredited business school. Preference will be given to candidates that are enthusiastic, collegial, engaged with students, good communicators, and team players. Questions may be addressed to Henry Xie, chair of the department, at xiey@cofc.edu.. Special Instructions to Applicants Formal applications for the position must be submitted through the College’s PeopleAdmin™ site at http://jobs.cofc.edu . Submit online (1) a letter of application, (2) a recent CV, (3) unofficial graduate transcripts (official transcripts will be required for hiring), (4) a one-page statement of your teaching philosophy, (5) names and contact information of three references and (6) optional teaching evaluations if available. The department will begin considering applications when an adjunct opportunity becomes available and will continue considering applicants until the position is filled. Please contact the Search Chair with questions. Is this position Grant funded? No EEO Statement The College of Charleston is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate against any individual or group on the basis of sex, gender (including gender identity and/or expression), pregnancy, race, religion, color, national origin, age, disability, military or veteran status, sexual orientation, genetic information, and other classifications protected by applicable federal, state, and local laws. For more information, please visit eop.cofc.edu . Quicklink for Posting https://jobs.cofc.edu/postings/18640 Reference Letters Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Chronicle of Higher Education CofC - Alumni Career Services College of Charleston Website Diverse: Issues in Higher Education Glassdoor Handshake HigherEdJobs Indeed.com Internal Job Posting jbcjobs (Joint Base Charleston Military & Family Readiness) Job Fair LinkedIn Monster.com Personal Referral Post and Courier Public Job Posting SC Works (SC Department of Employment and Workforce) Twitter Word of mouth Other National Labor Exchange CareerBuilder SpouseWorks Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Application Curriculum Vitae Teaching Philosophy Unofficial Graduate Transcripts Reference List Optional Documents Resume Unofficial Undergraduate Transcripts Student Course-Instructor Reviews Teaching Portfolio Syllabi Email: jobs@cofc.edu General Information: 843.953.5512 Mailing Address: 66 George St. Charleston, SC 29424 HR Office 160 Calhoun St. Lightsey Building B36 Charleston, SC 29424 Campus Maps ©2020 All Rights Reserved. Privacy Policy To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
