    "https://jobs.cofc.edu/postings/18723": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructor of Economics",
      "description": "College of Charleston Employment Site | Adjunct Instructor of Economics Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Applicant Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Academic Jobs Student Jobs Contact Us Adjunct Instructor of Economics Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Posting Details General Information Rank Adjunct Instructor FLSA Exempt Position Type Adjunct Internal Title Adjunct Instructor of Economics Department Economics School/Area School of Business Posting Number A2026030P Specialty and subspecialty, if any, sought Courses to be covered Econ 200 – Principles of Microeconomics (3 credit hours) Econ 201 – Principles of Macroeconomics (3 credit hours) Position Description The Department of Economics at the College of Charleston seeks an Adjunct Instructor of Economics to teach undergraduate economics courses, assess student learning, maintain accurate course records, hold appropriate office hours, and communicate effectively with students and department leadership. The successful candidate will demonstrate subject-matter expertise, a commitment to student-centered teaching, and the ability to use appropriate instructional technologies. A master’s degree in economics or a closely related field (including at least 18 graduate hours in economics or a closely related field) is required, and prior college-level teaching experience is preferred. Applicants should submit a resume and copies of all relevant transcripts in electronic form using the College of Charleston’s online application system at https://jobs.cofc.edu. Questions concerning the position should be addressed to Dr. Chris Mothorpe, Professor and Chair, at mothorpeca@cofc.edu. Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Special Instructions to Applicants Is this position Grant funded? No EEO Statement The College of Charleston is an equal opportunity employer and does not discr