    "https://jobs.cofc.edu/postings/18720": {
      "title": "Adjunct Lecturer of Archaeology",
      "description": "College of Charleston Employment Site | Adjunct Lecturer of Archaeology Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Applicant Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Academic Jobs Student Jobs Contact Us Adjunct Lecturer of Archaeology Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Applicants should have a master’s or doctoral degree in archaeology or a closely related field, with a minimum of 18 credit hours in graduate-level archaeology and closely-related courses, preferably with experience in teaching archaeological methods, regional expressions of past human culture with a focus on material evidence, or cultural heritage management. Posting Details General Information Rank Adjunct Lecturer FLSA Exempt Position Type Adjunct Internal Title Adjunct Lecturer of Archaeology Department SLCWA School/Area School of LCWA Posting Number A2026036P Specialty and subspecialty, if any, sought Archaeology: practices, methods, and theories; Archaeological interpretation; regional expressions of past human culture as evidenced through material remains Courses to be covered General education courses about archaeology in related disciplines (e.g. Anthropology) and/or upper-level electives in Archaeology or related disciplines as needed, commensurate with relevant degrees, research, and teaching experience. Position Description Adjunct lecturer in archaeology. Adjunct assignments are temporary, may be full-time or part-time, and/or immediate or as needed. This job posting is not for a specific assignment or for a full-time FTE faculty position, but rather for a pool of candidates who may be considered for teaching for the fall and spring semesters. Duties include teaching general education 100-level courses and upper-level courses as qualifications and demand warrant. Applicants may be credentialed in archaeology and/or in related fields with coursework and experience in archaeology. Special Instructions to Applicants Applicants should have a master’s or doctoral degree in archaeology or a closely related field, with a minimum of 18 credit hours in graduate-level archaeology and closely-related courses, preferably with experience in teaching archaeological methods, regional expressions of past human culture with a focus on material evidence, or cultural heritage management. Is this position Grant funded? No EEO Statement The College of Charleston is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate against any individual or group on the basis of sex, gender (including gender identity and/or expression), pregnancy, race, religion, color, national origin, age, disability, military or veteran status, sexual orientation, genetic information, and other classifications protected by applicable federal, state, and local laws. For more information, please visit eop.cofc.edu . Quicklink for Posting https://jobs.cofc.edu/postings/18660 Reference Letters Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Chronicle of Higher Education CofC - Alumni Career Services College of Charleston Website Diverse: Issues in Higher Education Glassdoor Handshake HigherEdJobs Indeed.com Internal Job Posting jbcjobs (Joint Base Charleston Military & Family Readiness) Job Fair LinkedIn Monster.com Personal Referral Post and Courier Public Job Posting SC Works (SC Department of Employment and Workforce) Twitter Word of mouth Other National Labor Exchange CareerBuilder SpouseWorks Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Application Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Teaching Philosophy Research and Professional Development Statement Sample Publication 1 Sample Publication 2 Sample Publication 3 Student Course-Instructor Reviews Teaching Portfolio Philosophy of Advising Statement Philosophy of Student Success & Retention Syllabi Email: jobs@cofc.edu General Information: 