    "https://jobs.cofc.edu/postings/18715": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of History (Civil War / Reconstruction)",
      "description": "College of Charleston Employment Site | Assistant Professor of History (Civil War / Reconstruction) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Applicant Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Academic Jobs Student Jobs Contact Us Assistant Professor of History (Civil War / Reconstruction) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Applications should be submitted electronically at https://jobs.cofc.edu/ by November 15, 2026. Applications should include 1) a cover letter outlining current and future research plans and teaching experience, 2) a current CV with names and contact information for three references, and 3) a writing sample of no more than 25 pages. The committee will request additional teaching materials from candidates selected for initial Zoom interviews. Please direct inquiries to Dr. Tammy Ingram, Associate Professor and search committee chair, at ingramt@cofc.edu . Posting Details POSTING INFORMATION Internal Title Assistant Professor of History (Civil War / Reconstruction) Position Type Tenure-track School/Area School of Humanities and Social Sciences Department History Position Description The Department of History at the College of Charleston invites applications for a full-time tenure-track appointment as Assistant Professor of the U.S. Civil War and Reconstruction Era, to begin August 2027. Candidates should be committed to excellence in undergraduate and graduate teaching as well as scholarly research. In addition to upper-level and graduate courses in the Civil War and Reconstruction and related topics, the ability to teach survey courses in the General Education curriculum in pre-modern and/or modern history is essential. All requirements for the Ph.D. in History must be completed by August 2027. Located in the heart of historic downtown Charleston, the College of Charleston is a public institution of 11,000 students with a commitment to excellence in teaching and research. The Department of History currently has more than three dozen faculty members with strong traditions of research engagement and innovative pedagogy. Faculty interests span a wide range of geographical areas and thematic perspectives, and the department promotes global thinking across the curriculum. For more information about the department, please see https://charleston.edu/history/ . Special Instructions to Applicants Applications should be submitted electronically at https://jobs.cofc.edu/ by November 15, 2026. Applications should include 1) a cover letter outlining current and future research plans and teaching experience, 2) a current CV with names and contact information for three references, and 3) a writing sample of no more than 25 pages. The committee will request additional teaching materials from candidates selected for initial Zoom interviews. Please direct inquiries to Dr. Tammy Ingram, Associate Professor and search committee chair, at ingramt@cofc.edu . Posting Date 10/13/2026 Closing Date 11/15/2026 Open Until Filled? No Posting Number F2026015P EEO Statement The College of Charleston is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate against any individual or group on the basis of sex, gender (including gender identity and/or expression), pregnancy, race, religion, color, national origin, age, disability, military or veteran status, sexual orientation, genetic information, and other classifications protected by applicable federal, state, and local laws. For more information, please visit https://charleston.edu/equal-opportunity-programs/ . Quicklink for Posting https://jobs.cofc.edu/postings/18635 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Chronicle of Higher Education CofC - Alumni Career Services College of Charleston Website Diverse: Issues in Higher Education Glassdoor Handshake HigherEdJobs Indeed.com Internal Job Pos