    "https://jobs.cofc.edu/postings/18702": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructor",
      "description": "College of Charleston Employment Site | Adjunct Instructor Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Applicant Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Academic Jobs Student Jobs Contact Us Adjunct Instructor Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Posting Details General Information Rank Adjunct Faculty Members FLSA Exempt Position Type Adjunct Internal Title Adjunct Instructor Department English School/Area School of Humanities and Social Sciences Posting Number A2026027P Specialty and subspecialty, if any, sought A number of MA degrees might qualify given the interdisciplinary field. Courses to be covered MEDH 200: Introduction to Medical Humanities Position Description The Medical Humanities program at the College of Charleston invites applications for an Adjunct Instructor for Spring 2027, with the possibility of renewal. Position Description The successful candidate will teach 1 to 2 in-person sections of Intro to Medical Humanities ( MEDH 200). This class provides students with a generalized background in the interdisciplinary field of Medical Humanities. Through lectures, readings, films, projects, and class discussions students will develop an understanding of and respect for the various ways scholars study and conceptualize human health and health experiences throughout time and space. As Medical Humanities draws from many fields, the course will explore a variety of scholarly perspectives, including history, philosophy, literary analysis, anthropology, sociology, psychology, and artistic presentation. Additionally, this course will endeavor to encourage and strengthen critical thinking and analytical skills in relation to, and across, these topics so that students are able to make meaningful interdisciplinary connections within both academic and non-academic settings. Minimum Qualifications An M.A. in a relevant field Teaching experience Preferred Qualifications Real-world experience in health settings that informs pedagogy Application Materials Letter of application Current CV, including contact information for two references About the Program The College of Charleston’s minor in Medical Humanities draws from a variety of departments, including history, English, anthropology, sociology, psychology, Latin-American studies, philosophy, women’s and gender studies, education, and public health. The minor approaches health, disease and medical care as culturally embedded human experiences that vary across time and place. Review of applications begins immediately and will continue until the position is filled. Special Instructions to Applicants Is this position Grant funded? No EEO Statement The College of Charleston is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate against any individual or group on the basis of sex, gender (including gender identity and/or expression), pregnancy, race, religion, color, national origin, age, disability, military or veteran status, sexual orientation, genetic information, and other classifications protected by applicable federal, state, and local laws. For more information, please visit eop.cofc.edu . Quicklink for Posting https://jobs.cofc.edu/postings/18551 Reference Letters Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Chronicle of Higher Education CofC - Alumni Career Services College of Charleston Website Diverse: Issues in Higher Education Glassdoor Handshake HigherEdJobs Indeed.com Internal Job Posting jbcjobs (Joint Base Charleston Military & Family Readiness) Job Fair LinkedIn Monster.com Personal Referral Post and Courier Public Job Posting SC Works (SC Department of Employment and Workforce) Twitter Word of mouth Other National Labor Exchange CareerBuilder SpouseWorks Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Application Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Email: jobs@cofc.edu General Information: 843.953.5512 Mailing Address: 66 George St. Charleston, SC 29424 HR Office 160 Calhoun St. Lightsey Building B36 Charleston, SC 29424 Campus Maps ©2020 All Rights Reserved. Privacy Policy To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
