    "https://jobs.cofc.edu/postings/18700": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructor of Hebrew",
      "description": "College of Charleston Employment Site | Adjunct Instructor of Hebrew Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Applicant Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Academic Jobs Student Jobs Contact Us Adjunct Instructor of Hebrew Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Applicants should submit: (1) a cover letter; (2) a CV that includes the names and contact information for three references; and (3) evidence of teaching effectiveness. For more information, contact Ashley Walters, Interim Director, Yaschik/Arnold Jewish Studies Program, College of Charleston, at waltersa1@cofc.edu . Posting Details General Information Rank Adjunct FLSA Exempt Position Type Adjunct Internal Title Adjunct Instructor of Hebrew Department Jewish Studies School/Area School of LCWA Posting Number A2026026P Specialty and subspecialty, if any, sought Hebrew language Courses to be covered Hebrew 101, Hebrew 102, Hebrew 201, Hebrew 202 Position Description The Yaschik/Arnold Jewish Studies Program at the College of Charleston invites applications for a part-time, non-tenure-track adjunct position beginning Spring 2027. We are seeking a dynamic and dedicated instructor with demonstrated excellence in teaching Modern Hebrew as a world language. The College of Charleston has a language requirement for all students, which can be satisfied by Hebrew coursework. Hebrew is also a core of the major and minor in Jewish Studies, as well as a key language in Middle Eastern and Islamic World Studies. Compensation is competitive and paid per course, in line with the College’s adjunct pay scale. Candidates must have a native or near-native command of Hebrew and a strong command of English. A master’s degree in Hebrew or a related pedagogical field is required. Prior teaching experience at the college level is preferred. The successful candidate will teach undergraduate Hebrew language courses (Hebrew 101, 102, 201, and 202) as needed each semester. The anticipated teaching load is two courses per semester, though this may vary depending on program needs and enrollment. The interdisciplinary faculty in the Yaschik/Arnold Jewish Studies Program have teaching and research interests that include the social sciences and humanities. The Program is also home to a vibrant student life community through Hillel. Applicants are encouraged to visit our program website https://charleston.edu/jewish/academics.php . To learn more about the College of Charleston, please visit www.charleston.edu . Special Instructions to Applicants Applicants should submit: (1) a cover letter; (2) a CV that includes the names and contact information for three references; and (3) evidence of teaching effectiveness. For more information, contact Ashley Walters, Interim Director, Yaschik/Arnold Jewish Studies Program, College of Charleston, at waltersa1@cofc.edu . Is this position Grant funded? No EEO Statement The College of Charleston is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate against any individual or group on the basis of sex, gender (including gender identity and/or expression), pregnancy, race, religion, color, national origin, age, disability, military or veteran status, sexual orientation, genetic information, and other classifications protected by applicable federal, state, and local laws. For more information, please visit eop.cofc.edu . Quicklink for Posting https://jobs.cofc.edu/postings/18517 Reference Letters Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Chronicle of Higher Education CofC - Alumni Career Services College of Charleston Website Diverse: Issues in Higher Education Glassdoor Handshake HigherEdJobs Indeed.com Internal Job Posting jbcjobs (Joint Base Charleston Military & Family Readiness) Job Fair LinkedIn Monster.com Personal Referral Post and Courier Public Job Posting SC Work