    "https://jobs.cofc.edu/postings/18693": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructor of Studio Art (painting / drawing)",
      "description": "College of Charleston Employment Site | Adjunct Instructor of Studio Art (painting / drawing) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Applicant Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Academic Jobs Student Jobs Contact Us Adjunct Instructor of Studio Art (painting / drawing) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Candidates must submit a portfolio of 20 artworks, 20 student works, a reference list, and a cover letter and CV. Posting Details General Information Rank Adjunct Instructor FLSA Exempt Position Type Adjunct Internal Title Adjunct Instructor of Studio Art (painting / drawing) Department Studio Arts School/Area School of the Arts Posting Number A2026021P Specialty and subspecialty, if any, sought Painting Courses to be covered Painting 1 and Painting 2, Drawing 1 and Drawing 2 Position Description The Department of Studio Art seeks applicants for our Painting/Drawing adjunct instructor pool, with the potential to teach 1-3 courses per semester. Contracts are on a semester-by-semester basis and are dependent on enrollment. Candidates must have an MFA with a focus in painting and at least one year of teaching experience outside of graduate school. The ability to teach perceptual oil painting with a focus on still life, landscape, and the figure is required. Candidates must be well-versed in historical and contemporary concepts in painting. Ability to teach introductory-level drawing is preferred. Special Instructions to Applicants Candidates must submit a portfolio of 20 artworks, 20 student works, a reference list, and a cover letter and CV. Is this position Grant funded? No EEO Statement The College of Charleston is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate against any individual or group on the basis of sex, gender (including gender identity and/or expression), pregnancy, race, religion, color, national origin, age, disability, military or veteran status, sexual orientation, genetic information, and other classifications protected by applicable federal, state, and local laws. For more information, please visit eop.cofc.edu . Quicklink for Posting https://jobs.cofc.edu/postings/18382 Reference Letters Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Chronicle of Higher Education CofC - Alumni Career Services College of Charleston Website Diverse: Issues in Higher Education Glassdoor Handshake HigherEdJobs Indeed.com Internal Job Posting jbcjobs (Joint Base Charleston Military & Family Readiness) Job Fair LinkedIn Monster.com Personal Referral Post and Courier Public Job Posting SC Works (SC Department of Employment and Workforce) Twitter Word of mouth Other National Labor Exchange CareerBuilder SpouseWorks Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Application Curriculum Vitae Slideshow of Personal Work (limited to 20 images) Slideshow of Student Work (limited to 20 images) Reference List Optional Documents Email: jobs@cofc.edu General Information: 843.953.5512 Mailing Address: 66 George St. Charleston, SC 29424 HR Office 160 Calhoun St. Lightsey Building B36 Charleston, SC 29424 Campus Maps ©2020 All Rights Reserved. Privacy Policy To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
