    "https://jobs.cofc.edu/postings/18691": {
      "title": "Adjunct Lecturer of Management and Entrepreneurship",
      "description": "College of Charleston Employment Site | Adjunct Lecturer of Management and Entrepreneurship Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Applicant Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Academic Jobs Student Jobs Contact Us Adjunct Lecturer of Management and Entrepreneurship Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Posting Details General Information Rank Adjunct Instructor FLSA Exempt Position Type Adjunct Internal Title Adjunct Lecturer of Management and Entrepreneurship Department Management and Entrepreneurship School/Area School of Business Posting Number A2026020P Specialty and subspecialty, if any, sought Management and Entrepreneurship Courses to be covered Position Description POSITION : The Department of Management and Entrepreneurship in the School of Business at the College of Charleston invites applications for an Adjunct Instructor position beginning August 16, 2026. The successful candidate will teach undergraduate and/or graduate courses in management, entrepreneurship, or closely related fields within the School of Business. Teaching responsibilities may include courses offered through the department’s undergraduate and graduate programs. QUALIFICATIONS : An MBA or equivalent master’s level degree from either AACSB , EFMD , or EQUIS -accredited programs is the minimum academic requirement for this position. Candidates should demonstrate relevant academic and/or professional expertise and a commitment to high-quality teaching. Preference will be given to candidates who are enthusiastic, collegial, engaged with students, good communicators, and team players. HOW TO APPLY : Formal applications for the position must be submitted through the College’s PeopleAdmin™ site at http://jobs.cofc.edu . Submit online (1) a letter of application, (2) a recent CV, (3) unofficial graduate transcripts (official transcripts will be required for hiring), (4) names and contact information for three references and (5) optional teaching evaluations if available. The department will begin considering applications on August 12, 2026, and will continue considering applicants until the position is filled. Please contact the Search Chair with questions. David Wyman, PhD Chair of the Search Committee Department of Management and Entrepreneurship School of Business College of Charleston Phone: 858-229-9028 wymandm@cofc.edu ABOUT THE SCHOOL OF BUSINESS : Founded in 1770, the College of Charleston is a public university grounded in the principles of the liberal arts and committed to developing ethically centered, intellectually versatile, and globally fluent citizens who create innovative solutions to social, economic, and environmental challenges. In its 2020 edition, U.S. News & World Report ranks the College as the No. 5 top public college in the South, the No. 3 ranked college for veterans among Southern institutions, the No. 8 most innovative school in the region, the No. 8 best college for undergraduate teaching in the south and a best value regional college. The School of Business at the College of Charleston is located in the heart of beautiful Charleston, a progressive city that has an emphasis on entrepreneurship and innovation. The School of Business is thriving with an active Board of Governors and access to community leaders. Visit the School’s website at https://sb.cofc.edu/ . Special Instructions to Applicants Is this position Grant funded? No EEO Statement The College of Charleston is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate against any individual or group on the basis of sex, gender (including gender identity and/or expression), pregnancy, race, religion, color, national origin, age, disability, military or veteran status, sexual orientation, genetic information, and other classifications protected by applicable federal, state, and local laws. For more information, please visit eop.cofc.edu . Quicklink for Posting https://jobs.cofc.edu/postings/18380 Reference Letters Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Chronicle of Higher Education CofC - Alumni Career Services College of Charleston Website Diverse: Issues in Higher Education Glassdoor Handshake HigherEdJobs Indeed.com Internal Job Posting jbcjobs (Joint Base Charleston Military & Family Readiness) Job Fair LinkedIn Monster.com Personal Referral Post and Courier Public Job Posting SC Works (SC Department of Employment and Workforce) Twitter Word of mouth Other National Labor Exchange CareerBuilder SpouseWorks Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Application Curriculum Vitae Unofficial Graduate Transcripts Reference List Optional Documents Teaching Philosophy Student Course-Instructor Reviews Email: jobs@cofc.edu General Information: 843.953.5512 Mailing Address: 66 George St. Charleston, SC 29424 HR Office 160 Calhoun St. Lightsey Building B36 Charleston, SC 29424 Campus Maps ©2020 All Rights Reserved. Privacy Policy To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.cofc.edu/postings/18690": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructor of Spanish or Portuguese",
      "description": "College of Charleston Employment Site | Adjunct Instructor of Spanish or Portuguese Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Applicant Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Academic Jobs Student Jobs Contact Us Adjunct Instructor of Spanish or Portuguese Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Posting Details General Information Rank Adjunct Instructor FLSA Exempt Position Type Adjunct Internal Title Adjunct Instructor of Spanish or Portuguese Department Hispanic Studies School/Area School of LCWA Posting Number A2026011P Specialty and subspecialty, if any, sought Master’s degree in Spanish, Portuguese, Hispanic Studies, Luso-Brazilian Studies, Spanish Linguistics, or a closely related field. At least 18 graduate credit hours in Spanish or Portuguese. Professional fluency in Spanish or Portuguese and English. Teaching experience at the postsecondary level, particularly in beginning Spanish or Portuguese language courses. Courses to be covered In-person introductory-level Spanish language courses: SPAN 101, SPAN 102, SPAN 190, SPAN 200, SPAN 201, SPAN 202. Occasionally classes in Portuguese classes will be available, such as PORT 101, PORT 102, PORT 201, PORT 202 or a 6-credit PORT 150 for PORT 250. Position Description Adjunct Lecturer of Spanish (or Portuguese) to teach in-person introductory-level language courses (e.g., SPAN 101 through SPAN 202) on our historic downtown Charleston campus. This is a part-time, non-tenure track faculty position for the Fall semester, with the possibility of renewal based on departmental needs and performance. We are seeking dynamic and student-focused educators committed to fostering basic Spanish or Portuguese language acquisition and cultural competence through communicative and inclusive teaching practices. Special Instructions to Applicants Is this position Grant funded? No EEO Statement The College of Charleston is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate against any individual or group on the basis of sex, gender (including gender identity and/or expression), pregnancy, race, religion, color, national origin, age, disability, military or veteran status, sexual orientation, genetic information, and other classifications protected by applicable federal, state, and local laws. For more information, please visit eop.cofc.edu . Quicklink for Posting https://jobs.cofc.edu/postings/18290 Reference Letters Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Chronicle of Higher Education CofC - Alumni Career Services College of Charleston Website Diverse: Issues in Higher Education Glassdoor Handshake HigherEdJobs Indeed.com Internal Job Posting jbcjobs (Joint Base Charleston Military & Family Readiness) Job Fair LinkedIn Monster.com Personal Referral Post and Courier Public Job Posting SC Works (SC Department of Employment and Workforce) Twitter Word of mouth Other National Labor Exchange CareerBuilder SpouseWorks Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Application Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Resume Teaching Philosophy Student Course-Instructor Reviews Reference List Email: jobs@cofc.edu General Information: 843.953.5512 Mailing Address: 66 George St. Charleston, SC 29424 HR Office 160 Calhoun St. Lightsey Building B36 Charleston, SC 29424 Campus Maps ©2020 All Rights Reserved. Privacy Policy To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
