    "https://jobs.cofc.edu/postings/18689": {
      "title": "Adjunct Lecturer of Finance and Real Estate",
      "description": "College of Charleston Employment Site | Adjunct Lecturer of Finance and Real Estate Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Applicant Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Academic Jobs Student Jobs Contact Us Adjunct Lecturer of Finance and Real Estate Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Applicants should hold a master's or doctoral degree in finance, real estate, or a closely related field, with at least 18 graduate credit hours in finance or real estate. Preference will be given to candidates with college-level teaching experience and/or substantial professional experience in a directly related field. Offers of employment are contingent upon a successful background check. All applications must be submitted online https://jobs.cofc.edu . Posting Details General Information Rank Adjunct Lecturer FLSA Exempt Position Type Adjunct Internal Title Adjunct Lecturer of Finance and Real Estate Department Finance School/Area School of Business Posting Number A2026014P Specialty and subspecialty, if any, sought Courses to be covered Finance or Real Estate courses as qualifications and demand warrant. Position Description Adjunct assignments are temporary, may be full-time or part-time, and/or immediate or as needed. This job posting is not for a specific assignment or for a full-time FTE faculty position, but rather for a pool of candidates who may be considered for teaching for the fall and spring semesters. Duties primarily include teaching a variety of finance and real estate courses as qualifications and demand warrant. Special Instructions to Applicants Applicants should hold a master’s or doctoral degree in finance, real estate, or a closely related field, with at least 18 graduate credit hours in finance or real estate. Preference will be given to candidates with college-level teaching experience and/or substantial professional experience in a directly related field. Offers of employment are contingent upon a successful background check. All applications must be submitted online https://jobs.cofc.edu . Is this position Grant funded? EEO Statement The College of Charleston is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate against any individual or group on the basis of sex, gender (including gender identity and/or expression), pregnancy, race, religion, color, national origin, age, disability, military or veteran status, sexual orientation, genetic information, and other classifications protected by applicable federal, state, and local laws. For more information, please visit eop.cofc.edu . Quicklink for Posting https://jobs.cofc.edu/postings/18315 Reference Letters Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Chronicle of Higher Education CofC - Alumni Career Services College of Charleston Website Diverse: Issues in Higher Education Glassdoor Handshake HigherEdJobs Indeed.com Internal Job Posting jbcjobs (Joint Base Charleston Military & Family Readiness) Job Fair LinkedIn Monster.com Personal Referral Post and Courier Public Job Posting SC Works (SC Department of Employment and Workforce) Twitter Word of mouth Other National Labor Exchange CareerBuilder SpouseWorks Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Application Curriculum Vitae Unofficial Graduate Transcripts Reference List Optional Documents Unofficial Undergraduate Transcripts Email: jobs@cofc.edu General Information: 843.953.5512 Mailing Address: 66 George St. Charleston, SC 29424 HR Office 160 Calhoun St. Lightsey Building B36 Charleston, SC 29424 Campus Maps ©2020 All Rights Reserved. Privacy Policy To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
