    "https://jobs.cofc.edu/postings/18688": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructor of Public Health",
      "description": "College of Charleston Employment Site | Adjunct Instructor of Public Health Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Applicant Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Academic Jobs Student Jobs Contact Us Adjunct Instructor of Public Health Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Posting Details General Information Rank Adjunct Faculty Members FLSA Exempt Position Type Adjunct Internal Title Adjunct Instructor of Public Health Department Department of Public Health Sciences and Administration School/Area School of Health Sciences Posting Number A2026012P Specialty and subspecialty, if any, sought Courses to be covered Position Description The Department of Public Health Sciences and Administration at the College of Charleston invites applications for an Adjunct Instructor of Public Health as an open application pool as needed by department. Position Description The successful candidate will teach courses relevant to their academic background and professional experience. Courses may include, by are not limited to, Introduction to Public Health, Personal and Community Health, Global Health, Epidemiology, and Biostatistics. Minimum Qualifications Master’s in Public Health or a closely related field Demonstrated teaching experience Strong commitment to student-centered pedagogy Preferred Qualifications Prior teaching experience at the college level as the instructor on record Application Materials Letter of application Current CV, including contact information for two references About the Department The Department of Public Health Sciences and Administration ( PHSA ) equips students to address today’s most pressing health issues through interdisciplinary coursework, applied learning, and hands-on experience. Our programs provide multiple pathways for students interested in improving population health, managing healthcare systems, and using data and technology to drive better outcomes. Majors and Minor: Public Health (BS) Public Health (BA) Health Services Administration and Management ( HSAM ) Health Informatics (Minor) Review of applications begins immediately and continues until the position is filled. Special Instructions to Applicants Is this position Grant funded? EEO Statement The College of Charleston is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate against any individual or group on the basis of sex, gender (including gender identity and/or expression), pregnancy, race, religion, color, national origin, age, disability, military or veteran status, sexual orientation, genetic information, and other classifications protected by applicable federal, state, and local laws. For more information, please visit eop.cofc.edu . Quicklink for Posting https://jobs.cofc.edu/postings/18299 Reference Letters Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Chronicle of Higher Education CofC - Alumni Career Services College of Charleston Website Diverse: Issues in Higher Education Glassdoor Handshake HigherEdJobs Indeed.com Internal Job Posting jbcjobs (Joint Base Charleston Military & Family Readiness) Job Fair LinkedIn Monster.com Personal Referral Post and Courier Public Job Posting SC Works (SC Department of Employment and Workforce) Twitter Word of mouth Other National Labor Exchange CareerBuilder SpouseWorks Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter / Letter of Application Optional Documents Curriculum Vitae Email: jobs@cofc.edu General Information: 843.953.5512 Mailing Address: 66 George St. Charleston, SC 29424 HR Office 160 Calhoun St. Lightsey Building B36 Charleston, SC 29424 Campus Maps ©2020 All Rights Reserved. Privacy Policy To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
