    "https://jobs.cofc.edu/postings/18683": {
      "title": "Instructor of Hebrew",
      "description": "College of Charleston Employment Site | Instructor of Hebrew Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Applicant Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Academic Jobs Student Jobs Contact Us Instructor of Hebrew Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Applicants should submit: (1) a cover letter; (2) a CV that includes the names and contact information for three references; and (3) a teaching philosophy and 4) evidence of teaching effectiveness (uploaded as Teaching Portfolio). For more information, contact Dr. Beth Meyer-Bernstein, Interim Director, Yaschik/Arnold Jewish Studies Program, College of Charleston at meyerbernsteine@cofc.edu . Posting Details POSTING INFORMATION Internal Title Instructor of Hebrew Position Type Instructor School/Area School of Languages, Cultures, and World Affairs Department Jewish Studies Position Description The Yaschik/Arnold Jewish Studies Program at the College of Charleston invites applications for a full-time position at the rank of Instructor of Hebrew beginning August 2026. We are seeking a dynamic and dedicated instructor with demonstrated excellence in teaching Modern Hebrew as a world language. The ideal candidate will also be interested and credentialed to teach interdisciplinary courses that expand our current offerings in the liberal arts. The College of Charleston has a two-year language requirement for all students, which can be satisfied by Hebrew coursework. Hebrew is also a core of the major and minor in Jewish Studies, as well as a key language in Middle Eastern and Islamic World Studies. During the sixth year, the candidate undergoes review for promotion to the rank of Senior Instructor. The position is benefits-eligible; the salary is competitive. Candidates must have a native or near-native command of Hebrew and a strong command of English. A master’s degree in Hebrew or a related pedagogical field is required, but a PhD at the time of appointment is preferred. Two years of teaching experience at the college level is also preferred. The ability to contribute to another program in LCWA is desirable. The successful candidate will teach undergraduate courses in Hebrew and develop classes that expand our current program offerings. The teaching load is twelve credit hours per semester to include at least two courses in Hebrew each semester. The interdisciplinary faculty in the Yaschik/Arnold Jewish Studies Program have teaching and research interests that include the social sciences and humanities. The Program is also home to a vibrant student life community through Hillel. Applicants are encouraged to visit our program website https://charleston.edu/jewish/academics.php . To learn more about the College of Charleston, please visit www.charleston.edu . Special Instructions to Applicants Applicants should submit: (1) a cover letter; (2) a CV that includes the names and contact information for three references; and (3) a teaching philosophy and 4) evidence of teaching effectiveness (uploaded as Teaching Portfolio). For more information, contact Dr. Beth Meyer-Bernstein, Interim Director, Yaschik/Arnold Jewish Studies Program, College of Charleston at meyerbernsteine@cofc.edu . Posting Date 10/01/2025 Closing Date 12/15/2025 Open Until Filled? Yes Posting Number F2016471P EEO Statement The College of Charleston is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate against any individual or group on the basis of sex, gender (including gender identity and/or expression), pregnancy, race, religion, color, national origin, age, disability, military or veteran status, sexual orientation, genetic information, and other classifications protected by applicable federal, state, and local laws. For more information, please visit eop.cofc.edu . Quicklink for Posting https://jobs.cofc.edu/postings/17190 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Chronicle of Higher Education CofC - Alumni Career Services College of Charleston Website Diverse: Issues in Higher Education Glassdoor Handshake HigherEdJobs Indeed.com Internal Job Posting jbcjobs (Joint Base Charleston Military & Family Readiness) Job Fair LinkedIn Monster.com Personal Referral Post and Courier Public Job Posting SC Works (SC Department of Employment and Workforce) Twitter Word of mouth Other National Labor Exchange CareerBuilder SpouseWorks Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Teaching Portfolio Cover Letter / Letter of Application Teaching Philosophy Optional Documents Email: jobs@cofc.edu General Information: 843.953.5512 Mailing Address: 66 George St. Charleston, SC 29424 HR Office 160 Calhoun St. Lightsey Building B36 Charleston, SC 29424 Campus Maps ©2020 All Rights Reserved. Privacy Policy To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.cofc.edu/postings/18680": {
      "title": "Dean, School of Education",
      "description": "College of Charleston Employment Site | Dean, School of Education Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Applicant Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Academic Jobs Student Jobs Contact Us Dean, School of Education Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Please see Special Instructions for more details. The Search Committee invites letters of nomination and applications (letter of interest, full resume/CV, and contact information of at least five references) to be submitted to the search firm assisting the University. Review of materials will begin immediately and continue until the appointment is made. It is preferred, however, that all nominations and applications are submitted before Wednesday, August 26, 2026. Please submit electronic applications directly to Parker Executive Search. For additional information, please contact: Porsha Williams, Vice President and Managing Director, Higher Education Jacob Anderson, Senior Principal Scott Gaffney, Associate Parker Executive Search Five Concourse Parkway, Suite 2875 | Atlanta, GA 30328 (770) 804-1996 x 111 pwilliams@parkersearch.com || janderson@parkersearch.com || sgaffney@parkersearch.com Posting Details POSTING INFORMATION Internal Title Dean, School of Education Position Type Tenured Administrative School/Area School of Education Department School of Education Dean's Office Position Description The School of Education has been preparing educators since 1937 and is dedicated to developing highly skilled, reflective practitioners equipped to meet the evolving needs of today’s classrooms. Through a combination of rigorous coursework, extensive clinical experiences, and strong partnerships with local school districts, the School prepares students to become effective teachers, leaders, and advocates in education. The Dean will partner with faculty, staff, students, and external stakeholders to advance the School’s mission of preparing innovative, reflective, and highly effective educators. The next Dean will provide strategic leadership to strengthen academic programs, expand partnerships with local and regional school systems, and elevate the School’s visibility and impact across South Carolina and beyond. Qualifications: • Demonstrated success in educator preparation • Experience with accreditation and regulatory standards in education • Proven ability to manage budgets, personnel, and complex academic operations • Record of fostering collaboration, innovation, and interdisciplinary initiatives • Experience navigating state and national policy environments impacting curriculum, licensure, educator preparation, and learning outcomes • Demonstrated success in fundraising, grants, or resource development • Deep understanding of the national landscape of schools of education, including trends in educator preparation, accreditation, and program innovation, along with knowledge of the South Carolina PK–12 and higher education landscape • Experience building partnerships with PK-12 systems, community organizations, and external stakeholders • Commitment to student success and faculty and staff development • Professional experience in PK–12 public school settings, such as teaching, school leadership, district administration, or related educational roles Special Instructions to Applicants The Search Committee invites letters of nomination and applications (letter of interest, full resume/CV, and contact information of at least five references) to be submitted to the search firm assisting the University. Review of materials will begin immediately and continue until the appointment is made. It is preferred, however, that all nominations and applications are submitted before Wednesday, August 26, 2026. Please submit electronic applications directly to Parker Executive Search. For additional information, please contact: Porsha Williams, Vice President and Managing Director, Higher Education Jacob Anderson, Senior Principal Scott Gaffney, Associate Parker Executive Search Five Concourse Parkway, Suite 2875 | Atlanta, GA 30328 (770) 804-1996 × 111 pwilliams@parkersearch.com || janderson@parkersearch.com || sgaffney@parkersearch.com Posting Date 10/14/2026 Closing Date Open Until Filled? Yes Posting Number F2026017P EEO Statement The College of Charleston is an Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity employer and does not discriminate against any individual or group on the basis of gender, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, age, race, color, religion, national origin, veteran status, genetic information, or disability. Quicklink for Posting https://jobs.cofc.edu/postings/18673 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Optional Documents Email: jobs@cofc.edu General Information: 843.953.5512 Mailing Address: 66 George St. Charleston, SC 29424 HR Office 160 Calhoun St. Lightsey Building B36 Charleston, SC 29424 Campus Maps ©2020 All Rights Reserved. Privacy Policy To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.cofc.edu/postings/18657": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Psychology (quantitative and/or experimental methodology)",
      "description": "College of Charleston Employment Site | Assistant Professor of Psychology (quantitative and/or experimental methodology) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Applicant Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Academic Jobs Student Jobs Contact Us Assistant Professor of Psychology (quantitative and/or experimental methodology) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details POSTING INFORMATION Internal Title Assistant Professor of Psychology (quantitative and/or experimental methodology) Position Type Tenure-track School/Area School of Humanities and Social Sciences Department Psychology Position Description ASSISTANT PROFESSOR . The Department of Psychology at the College of Charleston invites applications for a tenure-track faculty position in quantitative and/or experimental methodology at the assistant professor level beginning August 16, 2027. Candidates must have a Ph.D. in Psychology or a related field and be primarily interested in teaching statistics and research methods courses. Candidates must demonstrate a strong commitment to undergraduate teaching and maintaining an active research program within their area of specialization that is capable of involving undergraduate students. We are particularly interested in candidates who will complement the strengths of existing psychology faculty and whose primary area of research is feasible for student mentoring at the College of Charleston. Primary teaching responsibilities will include psychological statistics, psychological research methods, and advanced quantitative methods, with a typical semester load of 9 contact hours. Applicants with experience in open-science and/or advanced quantitative techniques, including but not limited to structural equation modeling, multilevel modeling, Bayesian estimation, psychometrics, or longitudinal designs, are encouraged to note this experience in their application materials. The College of Charleston , located in Charleston, SC, is a public institution of 11,000 students with a commitment to excellence in teaching and research. The College of Charleston boasts two renovated science facilities to support the research needs of the successful candidate. Furthermore, the Medical University of South Carolina ( MUSC ) and the Citadel are located a few blocks from the main campus and offer the opportunity for research collaboration. For more information on the College and Psychology Department, visit https://charleston.edu/psychology/index.php . Review of applications will begin on November 13th, 2026, and employment will begin on August 16, 2027. All applicants must submit a cover letter of application, curriculum vitae, research statement, teaching philosophy, up to three relevant publications, graduate transcript(s), and the names and contact information for three colleagues who can provide a recommendation. Applicants should highlight their experience and approach to mentoring students in their cover letter and teaching statement. Specific questions regarding the advertised position should be directed to Stephen Short, search committee chair, at shortsd@cofc.edu . This is a nine-month appointment; salary is competitive and commensurate with experience and qualifications. Special Instructions to Applicants Posting Date 10/12/2026 Closing Date 11/24/2026 Open Until Filled? No Posting Number F2026011P EEO Statement The College of Charleston is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate against any individual or group on the basis of sex, gender (including gender identity and/or expression), pregnancy, race, religion, color, national origin, age, disability, military or veteran status, sexual orientation, genetic information, and other classifications protected by applicable federal, state, and local laws. For more information, please visit eop.cofc.edu . Quicklink for Posting https://jobs.cofc.edu/postings/18612 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Application Curriculum Vitae Teaching Philosophy Research and Professional Development Statement Unofficial Graduate Transcripts Sample Publication 1 Optional Documents Resume Unofficial Undergraduate Transcripts Sample Publication 2 Sample Publication 3 Student Course-Instructor Reviews Teaching Portfolio Syllabi Email: jobs@cofc.edu General Information: 843.953.5512 Mailing Address: 66 George St. Charleston, SC 29424 HR Office 160 Calhoun St. Lightsey Building B36 Charleston, SC 29424 Campus Maps ©2020 All Rights Reserved. Privacy Policy To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.cofc.edu/postings/18656": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Psychology (sensory neuroscience)",
      "description": "College of Charleston Employment Site | Assistant Professor of Psychology (sensory neuroscience) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Applicant Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Academic Jobs Student Jobs Contact Us Assistant Professor of Psychology (sensory neuroscience) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details POSTING INFORMATION Internal Title Assistant Professor of Psychology (sensory neuroscience) Position Type Tenure-track School/Area School of Humanities and Social Sciences Department Psychology Position Description ASSISTANT PROFESSOR . The Department of Psychology at the College of Charleston invites applications for a tenure-track position in sensory neuroscience at the assistant professor level beginning August 16th, 2027. Applicants must have a Ph.D. in Psychology, Neuroscience, or a related field and demonstrate a strong commitment to undergraduate teaching and maintaining an active research program within their area of specialization that can involve undergraduate students. The specific research area within sensory neuroscience is open, and candidates specializing in animal models are especially encouraged to apply. We are particularly interested in candidates who will complement the strengths of existing psychology and neuroscience faculty and whose primary area of research is feasible for student mentoring at the College of Charleston. Primary teaching responsibilities will include foundational courses in Sensation & Perception and Behavioral Neuroscience, Advanced Laboratories in Sensation & Perception and/or Behavioral Neuroscience, specialized elective courses related to the candidate’s field of expertise, and other courses in the Psychology major. A typical semester load would normally involve 9 credit hours. The College of Charleston , located in Charleston, SC, is a public institution of 11,000 students with a commitment to excellence in teaching and research. The Medical University of South Carolina ( MUSC ) is located a few blocks from the main campus and offers the opportunity for research collaboration. For more information on the College and Psychology Department, visit https://charleston.edu/psychology/index.php . Review of applications will begin on November 12th, 2026. All applicants must submit a cover letter of application, curriculum vitae, research statement, teaching philosophy, up to three relevant publications, graduate transcript(s), and the names and contact information for three colleagues capable of providing a recommendation. Applicants should highlight their experience and approach to mentoring students in their cover letter and teaching statement. Specific questions regarding the advertised position should be directed to Jennifer Wilhelm, search committee chair, at wilhelmjc@cofc.edu . This is a nine-month appointment; salary is competitive and commensurate with experience and qualifications. Special Instructions to Applicants Posting Date 10/12/2026 Closing Date 11/12/2026 Open Until Filled? No Posting Number F2026012P EEO Statement The College of Charleston is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate against any individual or group on the basis of sex, gender (including gender identity and/or expression), pregnancy, race, religion, color, national origin, age, disability, military or veteran status, sexual orientation, genetic information, and other classifications protected by applicable federal, state, and local laws. For more information, please visit https://charleston.edu/equal-opportunity-programs/index.php . Quicklink for Posting https://jobs.cofc.edu/postings/18623 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Application Curriculum Vitae Teaching Philosophy Research and Professional Development Statement Unofficial Graduate Transcripts Sample Publication 1 Optional Documents Resume Unofficial Undergraduate Transcripts Sample Publication 2 Sample Publication 3 Student Course-Instructor Reviews Teaching Portfolio Reference List Syllabi Email: jobs@cofc.edu General Information: 843.953.5512 Mailing Address: 66 George St. Charleston, SC 29424 HR Office 160 Calhoun St. Lightsey Building B36 Charleston, SC 29424 Campus Maps ©2020 All Rights Reserved. Privacy Policy To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.cofc.edu/postings/18655": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Communication (media and strategic communication)",
      "description": "College of Charleston Employment Site | Assistant Professor of Communication (media and strategic communication) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Applicant Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Academic Jobs Student Jobs Contact Us Assistant Professor of Communication (media and strategic communication) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details POSTING INFORMATION Internal Title Assistant Professor of Communication (media and strategic communication) Position Type Tenure-track School/Area School of Humanities and Social Sciences Department Communication Position Description The Department of Communication at the College of Charleston invites applications for a full-time tenure-track position in media and strategic communication at the assistant professor level to begin August 2027. Candidates must have a Ph.D. in communication or a related field by August 2027, demonstrate a strong commitment to teaching, and maintain an active research agenda. We welcome candidates who examine media strategy from a range of theoretical and methodological perspectives. We are particularly interested in candidates who emphasize applied contexts such as science, sports, health, or other areas of public communication. Undergraduate teaching responsibilities include introductory survey courses in media studies and strategic communication, as well as upper-level courses aligned with the candidate’s area of expertise. Faculty members may also contribute to our professionally oriented master’s program. Review of applications will begin immediately, and applications must be submitted no later than November 16, 2026. All applicants must submit a letter of application, a curriculum vitae, and contact information for three colleagues capable of providing a recommendation. In their application letter, applicants should highlight their fit with the teacher-scholar model of higher education. Finalists may be asked to submit additional materials. The College of Charleston , located in Charleston, SC, is a public institution of 11,000 students with a commitment to excellence in teaching and research. The Department of Communication is home to over 600 majors, minors, and graduate students. The department’s two dozen full-time faculty members train students in speaking, writing, and media while teaching them to be more conscientious and ethical creators and consumers of communication messages. Faculty members bring their wide range of expertise to courses that closely align with their scholarly interests. Communication curriculum emphasizes experiential learning, including partnerships across the vibrant coastal city of Charleston. Department of Communication students and faculty members also partner with communications and media professionals through The Martin Center for Mentorship in Communication . Direct questions to Dr. Amanda Ruth-McSwain, search committee chair, at ruthmcswaina@charleston.edu. Salary is competitive and commensurate with experience and qualifications. Special Instructions to Applicants Posting Date 10/12/2026 Closing Date 11/16/2026 Open Until Filled? No Posting Number F2026014P EEO Statement The College of Charleston is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate against any individual or group on the basis of sex, gender (including gender identity and/or expression), pregnancy, race, religion, color, national origin, age, disability, military or veteran status, sexual orientation, genetic information, and other classifications protected by applicable federal, state, and local laws. For more information, please visit eop.cofc.edu . Quicklink for Posting https://jobs.cofc.edu/postings/18624 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Application Curriculum Vitae Reference List Optional Documents Other Document Email: jobs@cofc.edu General Information: 843.953.5512 Mailing Address: 66 George St. Charleston, SC 29424 HR Office 160 Calhoun St. Lightsey Building B36 Charleston, SC 29424 Campus Maps ©2020 All Rights Reserved. Privacy Policy To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
