    "https://jobs.cofc.edu/postings/18651": {
      "title": "Student Success Librarian",
      "description": "College of Charleston Employment Site | Student Success Librarian Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Applicant Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Academic Jobs Student Jobs Contact Us Student Success Librarian Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details POSTING INFORMATION Internal Title Student Success Librarian Position Type Tenure-track School/Area College of Charleston Libraries Department Library Position Description The Student Success Librarian at the College of Charleston Libraries is an adaptable and resourceful faculty member who plays a pivotal role in providing innovative and engaging library instruction to support the College’s strategic priorities for student retention, persistence, and graduation. This librarian will collaborate and engage with faculty and staff colleagues across the Libraries and the College to develop and deliver credit-bearing, scheduled, and point-of-need instruction that empowers users to locate, evaluate, and ethically use information resources within the ACRL Framework for Information Literacy for Higher Education. Additionally, this position supports first-year, transfer, and other at-promise student populations through targeted outreach and engagement initiatives. The Student Success Librarian is a tenure-track member of the library faculty. The salary range for this position is $70,000 to $74,000, commensurate with experience. Position Breakdown by Percentage of Effort Student Success and Engagement, 50% Cultivate and sustain collaborative relationships with other campus units and programs that support the College’s student success initiatives. Collaborate with the College’s Office for Student Success to analyze student success and engagement data to identify trends and target library outreach toward populations most in need of support. In consultation with other library units and campus offices, develop and deliver outreach programming, workshops, and orientation activities that connect first-year, transfer, and at-promise student populations to library services. Develop instructional materials, research guides, and online tutorials that support student learning objectives and promote lifelong learning skills. Instruction, 40% Design, deliver, and assess credit-bearing courses and scheduled instruction sessions that are student-focused, guided by the ACRL Framework for Information Literacy, and incorporate reflective teaching practices. Provide expert research assistance and point-of-need instruction to students, faculty, and staff through in-person and virtual consultations. Participate in library-wide assessment activities to evaluate the effectiveness of library instruction programs and services. Professional Growth and Development and Professional Service, 10% Undertake research and/or professional development related to professional and scholarly interests. Serve on library, College and professional committees, elected and assigned. Minimum Requirements Graduate degree in Library & Information Science (M.L.S. or equivalent) from an ALA -accredited program Strong public service orientation with an aptitude for providing online and face-to-face information literacy instruction and research services in an academic library Interest in student engagement and outreach Excellent interpersonal, presentation, and instructional technology skills Commitment to professional development and the ability to meet the research, teaching, service, and professional competency requirements for tenure and promotion advancement Some evening and/or weekend work may be required Preferred Qualifications Experience providing academic instruction. Experience evaluating, selecting, and implementing instructional technologies, strategies, or tools for universal access in an academic library setting, as well as knowledge of current issues and trends in pedagogy. Special Instructions to Applicants Posting Date 10/09/2026 Closing Date 11/30/2026 Open Until Filled? No Posting Number F2026013P EEO Statement The College of Charleston is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate against any individual or group on the basis of sex, gender (including gender identity and/or expression), pregnancy, race, religion, color, national origin, age, disability, military or veteran status, sexual orientation, genetic information, and other classifications protected by applicable federal, state, and local laws. For more information, please visit eop.cofc.edu . Quicklink for Posting https://jobs.cofc.edu/postings/18620 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Application Curriculum Vitae Teaching Philosophy Reference List Optional Documents Email: jobs@cofc.edu General Information: 843.953.5512 Mailing Address: 66 George St. Charleston, SC 29424 HR Office 160 Calhoun St. Lightsey Building B36 Charleston, SC 29424 Campus Maps ©2020 All Rights Reserved. Privacy Policy To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.cofc.edu/postings/18643": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Public Health",
      "description": "College of Charleston Employment Site | Assistant Professor of Public Health Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Applicant Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Academic Jobs Student Jobs Contact Us Assistant Professor of Public Health Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details POSTING INFORMATION Internal Title Assistant Professor of Public Health Position Type Tenure-track School/Area School of Health Sciences Department Department of Public Health Sciences and Administration Position Description The College of Charleston invites qualified applicants for a full-time, tenure-track Assistant Professor position within the Council on Education for Public Health ( CEPH ) accredited Public Health Program beginning in August 2027. The Public Health Program comprises a Bachelor of Science (B.S.) in Public Health and a Bachelor of Arts (B.A.) in Public Health, with concentrations in Global Health and Maternal and Child Health and is housed in the Department of Public Health Sciences and Administration within the expanding School of Health Sciences . The successful candidate will join an active department that also offers undergraduate degrees in Health Services Administration & Management. We currently have 12 full-time teacher-scholars that serve approximately 350 undergraduate majors. We are committed to preparing and equipping the next generation of health professionals and are seeking applicants who share our mission and want to engage with undergraduate students in and outside the classroom through dynamic teaching, professional advising, and research mentorship. Located in the heart of historic Charleston, South Carolina, the College of Charleston is a nationally recognized public university. Founded in 1770, the College is the oldest educational institution south of Virginia and the 13th oldest in the US. The College of Charleston is among the nation’s top universities for quality education, student life, and affordability. Its beautiful and historic campus, combined with contemporary facilities, cutting-edge programs, and accessible faculty, attracts students from across the US and around the world. Over 10,000 undergraduates and approximately 500 graduate students at the College enjoy a small campus feel blended with the advantages and diversity of a mid-sized, urban university. Students work closely with a committed faculty that is made up of more than 500 distinguished teacher-scholars. And the city of Charleston – world-renowned for its history, architecture, culture, and coastal environment – serves as a living and learning laboratory for experiences in business, science, technology, teaching, the humanities, languages, and the arts. The responsibilities of an Assistant Professor include 1) providing high-quality instruction in three course sections per semester within the Public Health Program, two of which will cover sections of PBHL 257: Principles of Human Nutrition, 2) maintaining an independent research agenda at the level of expectation for a tenure-track faculty member, 3) offering academic advising and professional mentoring for public health majors, 4) engaging in professional service activities, 5) working collaboratively within the program and department to help meet stated goals and objectives, and 6) committing to a liberal arts and sciences undergraduate education. Applicants must possess an earned PhD degree in public health or closely related discipline from an accredited institution by August 15, 2027. Applicants must be able to demonstrate the ability to teach undergraduate-level students with the promise of teaching excellence. We welcome applicants with research expertise in public health and human nutrition; applicants should show scholarly promise through authorship on professional presentations and peer-reviewed publications in relevant journals. Lastly, we prefer those with additional relevant professional certifications, a record of service, and/or mentoring students through the research process within a higher education setting. Interested individuals should apply online at https://jobs.cofc.edu /, and include a 1) curriculum vitae, 2) cover letter that describes your research agenda and outlines potential research collaborations in addition to a teaching philosophy that includes courses capable of and interested in instructing, 3) graduate transcripts, and 4) contact information for three references. Questions regarding the position can be directed to the search chair, Dr. Katie Trejo Tello, at mcinvaleke@cofc.edu. Applications completed by December 31st, 2026, will receive full consideration by the search committee. This is a continuing nine-month position; the salary and benefits package is competitive and commensurate with experience and qualifications. Special Instructions to Applicants Posting Date 10/05/2026 Closing Date 01/15/2027 Open Until Filled? No Posting Number F2026010P EEO Statement The College of Charleston is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate against any individual or group on the basis of sex, gender (including gender identity and/or expression), pregnancy, race, religion, color, national origin, age, disability, military or veteran status, sexual orientation, genetic information, and other classifications protected by applicable federal, state, and local laws. For more information, please visit eop.cofc.edu . Quicklink for Posting https://jobs.cofc.edu/postings/18537 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Application Curriculum Vitae Unofficial Graduate Transcripts Reference List Optional Documents Email: jobs@cofc.edu General Information: 843.953.5512 Mailing Address: 66 George St. Charleston, SC 29424 HR Office 160 Calhoun St. Lightsey Building B36 Charleston, SC 29424 Campus Maps ©2020 All Rights Reserved. Privacy Policy To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.cofc.edu/postings/18560": {
      "title": "Chair and Associate or Full Professor of French, Francophone, and Italian Studies",
      "description": "College of Charleston Employment Site | Chair and Associate or Full Professor of French, Francophone, and Italian Studies Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Applicant Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Academic Jobs Student Jobs Contact Us Chair and Associate or Full Professor of French, Francophone, and Italian Studies Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details POSTING INFORMATION Internal Title Chair and Associate or Full Professor of French, Francophone, and Italian Studies Position Type Tenured Administrative School/Area School of Languages, Cultures, and World Affairs Department French, Francophone, and Italian St Position Description The College of Charleston seeks a dynamic scholar, teacher, and academic leader at the rank of associate or full professor to serve as Chair of the Department of French, Francophone, and Italian Studies. The successful candidate will bring a strategic vision for the department, strong communication and leadership skills, and a demonstrated commitment to fostering a participatory and supportive environment. The chair will lead efforts in curricular innovation, faculty development, student success, and the continued enhancement of the department’s national reputation. The chair will hold a full-time, tenured faculty appointment in the Department of French, Francophone, and Italian Studies within the School of Languages, Cultures, and World Affairs. Candidates should have expertise in French, Francophone, or Italian Studies, or a closely related field, along with a distinguished record of research, publication, and teaching sufficient for appointment with tenure at the rank of associate or full professor. The position offers a competitive salary and a teaching load commensurate with administrative responsibilities. French, Francophone, and Italian Studies is a dynamic and vibrant department that enrolls approximately 1,000 students per semester and offers majors in French and Francophone Studies and French Teacher Education, as well as minors in French and Italian Studies. Many students combine this program with majors such as International Business, Hospitality and Tourism Management, Marketing, and International Studies. The department offers students a range of enrichment opportunities, including study abroad programs, experiential learning, student clubs, and residence in the historic French House. Please submit a cover letter, a CV, and contact information for three references by October 15, 2026. The successful candidate will demonstrate a record of academic leadership and program development as well as collegiality, professionalism, and the ability to work collaboratively with faculty, staff, and students. For more information, contact Dr. Aimee Arias, Dean, School of Languages, Cultures, and World Affairs, College of Charleston, 11 Glebe St., Charleston, SC 29424. ariasak@cofc.edu . Applicants are encouraged to visit the department website https://charleston.edu/french-italian-studies/ . To learn more about the College of Charleston, please visit www.charleston.edu . Special Instructions to Applicants Posting Date 09/21/2026 Closing Date 11/02/2026 Open Until Filled? No Posting Number F2026009P EEO Statement The College of Charleston is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate against any individual or group on the basis of sex, gender (including gender identity and/or expression), pregnancy, race, religion, color, national origin, age, disability, military or veteran status, sexual orientation, genetic information, and other classifications protected by applicable federal, state, and local laws. For more information, please visit eop.cofc.edu . Quicklink for Posting https://jobs.cofc.edu/postings/18463 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Application Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Teaching Philosophy Research and Professional Development Statement Unofficial Graduate Transcripts Other Document Teaching Portfolio Email: jobs@cofc.edu General Information: 843.953.5512 Mailing Address: 66 George St. Charleston, SC 29424 HR Office 160 Calhoun St. Lightsey Building B36 Charleston, SC 29424 Campus Maps ©2020 All Rights Reserved. Privacy Policy To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.cofc.edu/postings/18466": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Chemistry and Biochemistry (organic)",
      "description": "College of Charleston Employment Site | Assistant Professor of Chemistry and Biochemistry (organic) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Applicant Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Academic Jobs Student Jobs Contact Us Assistant Professor of Chemistry and Biochemistry (organic) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details POSTING INFORMATION Internal Title Assistant Professor of Chemistry and Biochemistry (organic) Position Type Tenure-track School/Area School of Natural and Environmental Sciences Department Chemistry Position Description Tenure-Track Assistant Professor in Organic Chemistry. The Department of Chemistry and Biochemistry at the College of Charleston invites applications for a tenure-track faculty position beginning in Fall 2027. A Ph.D. in organic chemistry or in a related discipline is required. We seek a dynamic teacher-scholar who will contribute to our ACS -approved program by teaching organic chemistry and developing advanced undergraduate courses in their area of expertise. The successful candidate will also establish an active research program that engages undergraduate students and promotes collaboration with the nearby Medical University of South Carolina ( MUSC ). Candidates with expertise in research areas that complement our departmental strengths, such as computational chemistry, toxicology, and pharmaceutical chemistry, are especially encouraged to apply. The successful candidate will benefit from our participation in the NIH -funded SC- INBRE network, which provides extensive opportunities to support biomedical research. Applications must be submitted via the electronic portal at jobs.cofc.edu . Complete applications must contain a cover letter, a curriculum vitae, a statement of teaching philosophy, a description of the proposed research, unofficial undergraduate and graduate transcripts, and three letters of recommendation. Review of applications will begin on September 10, 2026, and will continue until the position is filled. For more information, contact Dr. Tim Barker ( barkertj@cofc.edu ), Department of Chemistry & Biochemistry, College of Charleston, 66 George St., Charleston, SC 29424. Special Instructions to Applicants Posting Date 07/15/2026 Closing Date 11/02/2026 Open Until Filled? No Posting Number F2016501P EEO Statement Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity Employer: The College of Charleston is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate against any individual or group on the basis of sex, gender (including gender identity and/or expression), pregnancy, race, religion, color, national origin, age, disability, military or veteran status, sexual orientation, genetic information, and other classifications protected by applicable federal, state, and local laws. For more information, please visit eop.cofc.edu . Quicklink for Posting https://jobs.cofc.edu/postings/17937 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Application Curriculum Vitae Teaching Philosophy Research and Professional Development Statement Unofficial Undergraduate Transcripts Unofficial Graduate Transcripts Optional Documents Other Document Email: jobs@cofc.edu General Information: 843.953.5512 Mailing Address: 66 George St. Charleston, SC 29424 HR Office 160 Calhoun St. Lightsey Building B36 Charleston, SC 29424 Campus Maps ©2020 All Rights Reserved. Privacy Policy To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.cofc.edu/postings/18313": {
      "title": "Instructor of Dance",
      "description": "College of Charleston Employment Site | Instructor of Dance Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Applicant Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Academic Jobs Student Jobs Contact Us Instructor of Dance Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details POSTING INFORMATION Internal Title Instructor of Dance Position Type Instructor School/Area School of the Arts Department Theatre & Dance Position Description Full-time Instructor of Dance, Non-Tenure-Track COLLEGE OF CHARLESTON is accepting applications for a full-time, nine-month, non-tenure track appointment in the Department of Theatre and Dance. This appointment begins January 1, 2027. This is a full-time permanent position with a teaching load of four courses per semester. In the sixth year, the Instructor undergoes review for promotion to Senior Instructor. The Department of Theatre and Dance is NAST -accredited, offering BA and MAT degrees in Theatre and a BA in Dance. We seek a candidate who can inspire both beginning and experienced students in their initial dance studies and actively support the ongoing development of the Dance major. Regularly taught courses will serve as an entry point to dance students new to the department and those completing General Education requirements. The ideal candidate will bring expertise in one or more areas of dance technique, as well as the ability to teach non-Western dance practices, somatics, and/or theory-based courses. Responsibilities include teaching a full course load each semester (4/4); providing service to the department through recruitment efforts and serving on departmental committees; maintaining a record of professional development and sustained pedagogy; serving as an academic advisor to dance majors; guiding and assisting student participation in various conferences and festivals; and potentially choreographing for department productions as needed. Qualifications: MA, MFA , or PhD required by January 1, 2027; Professional experience/scholarship in dance; Prior undergraduate teaching experience strongly preferred. The ideal candidate is a dynamic educator passionate about mentoring students in a liberal arts program, possessing either an MFA or a PhD in Dance or a closely related discipline; has a minimum of three years’ experience teaching in post-secondary education; and has prior experience in student recruitment/advising/mentorship. Candidates who are currently active in and contributing to the dance field, either in traditional modes of scholarship or through creative practice, are preferred. Review of applications begins September 15, 2026. The College is located in historic downtown Charleston in a coastal metropolitan area of 750,000. Additional information about the institution and the surrounding area is available at https://www.cofc.edu/ . The College of Charleston is a nationally recognized public liberal arts and sciences university located in the heart of historic Charleston, SC. Since our founding in 1770, we have maintained a strong liberal arts curriculum. The College is a state-supported, comprehensive institution and ranks among the nation’s top universities in providing quality education in the arts, sciences, education, and business. No other university has the unique combination of our exceptional faculty, diverse programs, historic campus, coastal location, modern facilities, and cutting-edge programs. The student body numbers over 11,000 students in undergraduate and graduate programs combined. Special Instructions to Applicants Posting Date 07/29/2026 Closing Date Open Until Filled? Yes Posting Number F2026008P EEO Statement The College of Charleston is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate against any individual or group on the basis of sex, gender (including gender identity and/or expression), pregnancy, race, religion, color, national origin, age, disability, military or veteran status, sexual orientation, genetic information, and other classifications protected by applicable federal, state, and local laws. For more information, please visit eop.cofc.edu . Quicklink for Posting https://jobs.cofc.edu/postings/18272 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Application Curriculum Vitae Teaching Philosophy Optional Documents Link to sizzle reel (on Vimeo or YouTube) Email: jobs@cofc.edu General Information: 843.953.5512 Mailing Address: 66 George St. Charleston, SC 29424 HR Office 160 Calhoun St. Lightsey Building B36 Charleston, SC 29424 Campus Maps ©2020 All Rights Reserved. Privacy Policy To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.cofc.edu/postings/18188": {
      "title": "Associate or Full Professor of Real Estate / Director of the Carter Real Estate Center",
      "description": "College of Charleston Employment Site | Associate or Full Professor of Real Estate / Director of the Carter Real Estate Center Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Applicant Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Academic Jobs Student Jobs Contact Us Associate or Full Professor of Real Estate / Director of the Carter Real Estate Center Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Please see Special Instructions for more details. Greenwood Asher & Associates is assisting the College of Charleston in this search. Initial screening of applications will begin immediately and continue until an appointment is made. For best consideration, application materials should be submitted by October 5, 2026. Applications should include: A letter of interest addressing relevant experience and leadership approach; and A current CV or résumé. Materials should be submitted via: Candidate Portal Nominations and inquiries may be directed to: Jeremy Duff, Vice President for Executive Search – jeremyduff@greenwoodsearch.com Shelley Feather, Senior Executive Search Consultant – shelleyfeather@greenwoodsearch.com Greenwood Asher & Associates | greenwoodsearch.com Posting Details POSTING INFORMATION Internal Title Associate or Full Professor of Real Estate / Director of the Carter Real Estate Center Position Type Tenured Administrative School/Area School of Business Department Finance Position Description Buono Endowed Professor of Real Estate The College of Charleston’s School of Business invites applications and nominations for the inaugural Buono Endowed Professor of Real Estate. This is a distinctive opportunity for an accomplished scholar and industry-engaged leader to shape real estate education in a city renowned for its dynamic commercial real estate market and historic appeal. The Buono Endowed Professor will provide academic leadership for the Commercial Real Estate Finance program and may serve as Director of the Carter Real Estate Center. This position offers an exceptional platform for advancing innovative teaching, research, and impactful partnerships within the College and industry. About the Institution The College of Charleston is a nationally recognized public university located in the heart of historic Charleston, South Carolina. Founded in 1770, the institution is known for its strong liberal arts curriculum, vibrant campus community, and commitment to producing ethically centered, innovative, and globally fluent graduates. With a beautiful campus, contemporary facilities, and more than 11,000 students from across the U.S. and around the world, the College of Charleston offers a distinctive environment that blends tradition with forward-thinking education and fosters meaningful connections with the historic city it calls home. Key Responsibilities The Buono Endowed Professor will provide academic leadership for the Commercial Real Estate Finance program and may serve as Director of the Carter Real Estate Center. This position offers an exceptional platform for advancing innovative teaching, research, and impactful partnerships within the College and industry. Guide the enhancement and delivery of real estate curriculum, with a focus on experiential learning and career outcomes. Mentor students and support their placement into rewarding real estate career Foster collaborations with industry partners and the community. Lead and expand the Carter Real Estate Center’s educational and research initiatives Qualifications and Experience The successful candidate will join a a dynamic Department of Finance that is deeply committed to student success and experiential learning and should have the following qualifications. Doctorate in Real Estate, Finance, or a closely related field from an accredited institution; Significant professional experience in commercial real estate preferred; Demonstrated excellence in teaching and a strong record of scholarly research, including publication in respected journals; and Commitment to student development and mentoring junior faculty. Preferred qualifications include: Extensive professional experience in commercial real estate; Demonstrated excellence in teaching with the ability to teach courses such as Real Estate Finance and Investment; A strong record of scholarly research with the ability to mentor and engage junior faculty in research activities; Evidence of publication in reputable real estate and/or finance journals; and Prior service experience at the department, college, university, and/or professional community level. Application and Nomination Process Greenwood Asher & Associates is assisting the College of Charleston in this search. Initial screening of applications will begin immediately and continue until an appointment is made. For best consideration, application materials should be submitted by October 5, 2026. Applications should include: A letter of interest addressing relevant experience and leadership approach; and A current CV or résumé. Materials should be submitted via: Candidate Portal Nominations and inquiries may be directed to: Jeremy Duff, Vice President for Executive Search – jeremyduff@greenwoodsearch.com Shelley Feather, Senior Executive Search Consultant – shelleyfeather@greenwoodsearch.com Greenwood Asher & Associates | greenwoodsearch.com Special Instructions to Applicants Greenwood Asher & Associates is assisting the College of Charleston in this search. Initial screening of applications will begin immediately and continue until an appointment is made. For best consideration, application materials should be submitted by October 5, 2026. Applications should include: A letter of interest addressing relevant experience and leadership approach; and A current CV or résumé. Materials should be submitted via: Candidate Portal Nominations and inquiries may be directed to: Jeremy Duff, Vice President for Executive Search – jeremyduff@greenwoodsearch.com Shelley Feather, Senior Executive Search Consultant – shelleyfeather@greenwoodsearch.com Greenwood Asher & Associates | greenwoodsearch.com Posting Date 07/01/2026 Closing Date 10/30/2026 Open Until Filled? No Posting Number F2026005P EEO Statement The College of Charleston is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate against any individual or group on the basis of sex, gender (including gender identity and/or expression), pregnancy, race, religion, color, national origin, age, disability, military or veteran status, sexual orientation, genetic information, and other classifications protected by applicable federal, state, and local laws. For more information, please visit eop.cofc.edu. Quicklink for Posting https://jobs.cofc.edu/postings/18131 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Optional Documents Email: jobs@cofc.edu General Information: 843.953.5512 Mailing Address: 66 George St. Charleston, SC 29424 HR Office 160 Calhoun St. Lightsey Building B36 Charleston, SC 29424 Campus Maps ©2020 All Rights Reserved. Privacy Policy To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.cofc.edu/postings/18119": {
      "title": "Chair of the Engineering Department",
      "description": "College of Charleston Employment Site | Chair of the Engineering Department Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Applicant Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Academic Jobs Student Jobs Contact Us Chair of the Engineering Department Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Review of applications will begin on August 20 and will continue until the position is filled. Posting Details POSTING INFORMATION Internal Title Chair of the Engineering Department Position Type Tenure-track School/Area School of Engineering, Computer Science, and Mathematics Department Engineering Position Description The School of Engineering, Computing, and Mathematics ( SECM ) at the College of Charleston invites applications for a tenured position as Chair of the Department of Engineering at the rank of Associate Professor or Professor, with an anticipated start date of January 2026. Appointment rank and tenure status will be based on the candidate’s qualifications and experience. The successful candidate will provide visionary leadership to guide the department’s continued growth in academic programs, student enrollment, and national reputation. Candidates must demonstrate a strong commitment to excellence in undergraduate and graduate education, high-quality teaching, and maintaining an active, productive research agenda. Established in 2023, the Department of Engineering currently offers Bachelor of Science degrees in Electrical Engineering and Systems Engineering. A new interdisciplinary Bachelor of Science (BS) degree in Integrated Engineering and Business is in development, and a Biomedical Engineering program is currently in the early planning stages. This position presents a unique opportunity for an innovative leader to shape a young and evolving department during an exciting period of strategic expansion. SECM offers a friendly, dynamic, and collaborative environment, with ample opportunities for interdisciplinary partnerships across the university’s ten schools, including the Schools of Business, Education, Natural & Environmental Sciences, and the newly formed School of Health Sciences. The university is located just blocks from the Medical University of South Carolina ( MUSC ), providing opportunities for collaboration in medical and health-related education and research. Additionally, South Carolina is home to a growing industrial base, including leading manufacturers and a vibrant medical device and healthcare industry. Major Responsibilities Provide effective, cohesive, and collaborative leadership for a multi-disciplinary department, prioritizing strategies for student success and academic distinction Develop strategic vision and planning for the department, supporting the university’s goal to become a transformative national university that redefines liberal arts education through innovation Develop and maintain the enrollment and student success goals for each program Develop and oversee the department budget Manage course schedules and instructor assignments Foster professional growth and development of faculty and staff members within the department Oversee curriculum development and revisions for the department Assess academic programs offered by the department, ensuring the academic quality and rigor of the programs are maintained and continuously improved Attain and maintain professional accreditation where appropriate Foster cooperative and collaborative relationships and activities with other departments and units in the university Create and maintain collaborations with industry and other external partners Oversee an effective industrial advisory board Required Qualifications Applicants must hold a PhD or equivalent in engineering. Priority will be given to candidates with expertise in systems engineering, mechanical engineering, robotics, mechatronics, or a related field. Candidates must be eligible for appointment with tenure at the rank of Associate Professor or Professor A strong commitment to undergraduate education A record of scholarship commensurate with rank sought At least 7 years of experience in an academic setting Prior experience in academic leadership roles, such as department chair or director of a program Knowledge and appreciation of a variety of engineering disciplines, as well as disciplines across the academy Experience with ABET accreditation Curriculum and lab development experience Excellent communication and interpersonal skills Preferred Qualifications Interdisciplinary experience inside and outside of engineering disciplines Program development experience Experience working with industry and external partners Application Instructions Qualified candidates should submit their application package at https://jobs.cofc.edu/postings/16853 , including: Letter of application addressing your fit with the position and the College of Charleston Curriculum vitae Statements of teaching, research, and leadership philosophies Names and contact information for three references For more information, contact: Dr. Tom Kunkle, Chair of the Search Committee, Department of Mathematics and Statistics School of Engineering, Computing, and Mathematics 66 George Street, Charleston, SC 29424-0001 Email: kunklet@cofc.edu About the College of Charleston and the School of Engineering, Computing, and Mathematics: Founded in 1770, the College of Charleston is a public university grounded in the principles of the liberal arts and committed to developing intellectually versatile and globally fluent citizens who create innovative solutions to social, economic, and technological challenges. A primarily undergraduate institution with strong graduate degree programs, the university prides itself on excellence in education. The university enrolls over 10,000 undergraduate and 1000 graduate students. In its 2025 edition, U.S. News & World Report ranks the College as the No. 4 top public university in the south, the No. 5 ranked college for veterans among southern institutions, the No. 9 most innovative school in the region, and the No. 3 best college for undergraduate teaching in the south and a best value regional college. The College is in the heart of beautiful Charleston. Visit the College’s website at https://www.cofc.edu . Visit the School’s website at https://charleston.edu/school-engineering-computing-mathematics/ . Special Instructions to Applicants Review of applications will begin on August 20 and will continue until the position is filled. Posting Date 07/15/2025 Closing Date Open Until Filled? Yes Posting Number F2016457P EEO Statement The College of Charleston is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate against any individual or group on the basis of sex, gender (including gender identity and/or expression), pregnancy, race, religion, color, national origin, age, disability, military or veteran status, sexual orientation, genetic information, and other classifications protected by applicable federal, state, and local laws. For more information, please visit eop.cofc.edu. Quicklink for Posting https://jobs.cofc.edu/postings/16853 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Optional Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Application Curriculum Vitae Teaching Philosophy Research and Professional Development Statement Reference List Statement of Leadership Philosophy Email: jobs@cofc.edu General Information: 843.953.5512 Mailing Address: 66 George St. Charleston, SC 29424 HR Office 160 Calhoun St. Lightsey Building B36 Charleston, SC 29424 Campus Maps ©2020 All Rights Reserved. Privacy Policy To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.cofc.edu/postings/17676": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Mathematics",
      "description": "College of Charleston Employment Site | Assistant Professor of Mathematics Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Applicant Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Academic Jobs Student Jobs Contact Us Assistant Professor of Mathematics Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Please see Special Instructions for more details. Applications will be accepted at Mathjobs.org. Position details and application instructions can be found at <Mathjobs_listing_URL>. Posting Details POSTING INFORMATION Internal Title Assistant Professor of Mathematics Position Type Tenure-track School/Area School of Sciences and Mathematics Department Mathematics Position Description The College of Charleston Department of Mathematics and Statistics invites applications for a tenure-track assistant professor position beginning August 2025. Candidates in applied mathematics, ideally ones with expertise in numerical analysis, are preferred. Applicants must possess a Ph.D. in mathematics or a mathematical science by the employment start date. Since teaching, research and service make up the primary responsibilities of the position, a record of and potential for excellence in these areas, including directing undergraduate and graduate student research, make up the basis for ranking candidates. A complete application must contain: a cover letter, curriculum vita, teaching philosophy, current and projected research agenda, and at least three letters of recommendation, at least one addressing teaching. Questions regarding the position can be directed to Dr. Tom Kunkle, search committee chair, at kunklet@charleston.edu. This is a nine-month appointment; salary is competitive and commensurate with experience and qualifications. The review of applications will begin immediately, and applications will be considered until the position is filled. Special Instructions to Applicants Applications will be accepted at Mathjobs.org. Position details and application instructions can be found at <Mathjobs_listing_URL>. Posting Date 10/08/2024 Closing Date 02/16/2026 Open Until Filled? Yes Posting Number F2016432P EEO Statement The College of Charleston is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate against any individual or group on the basis of sex, gender (including gender identity and/or expression), pregnancy, race, religion, color, national origin, age, disability, military or veteran status, sexual orientation, genetic information, and other classifications protected by applicable federal, state, and local laws. For more information, please visit eop.cofc.edu . Quicklink for Posting https://jobs.cofc.edu/postings/15978 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Optional Documents Email: jobs@cofc.edu General Information: 843.953.5512 Mailing Address: 66 George St. Charleston, SC 29424 HR Office 160 Calhoun St. Lightsey Building B36 Charleston, SC 29424 Campus Maps ©2020 All Rights Reserved. Privacy Policy To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
