    "https://jobs.cofc.edu/postings/18762": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructor of Urban Studies",
      "description": "College of Charleston Employment Site | Adjunct Instructor of Urban Studies Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Applicant Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Academic Jobs Student Jobs Contact Us Adjunct Instructor of Urban Studies Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Posting Details General Information Rank Adjunct Instructor FLSA Non-Exempt Position Type Adjunct Internal Title Adjunct Instructor of Urban Studies Department School of Humanities and Social Sciences (Admin) School/Area School of Humanities and Social Sciences Posting Number A2026041P Specialty and subspecialty, if any, sought Several MA degrees would qualify given the interdisciplinary nature of the program, (e.g., Master in Public Administration, Master in Urban Studies, Master in Urban Geography, etc.) Courses to be covered URST 310 Urban Planning Position Description The Urban Studies program at the College of Charleston invites applications for an Adjunct Instructor for Spring 2027, with the possibility of renewal. Position Description The successful candidate will teach 1 in-person section of Urban Planning, URST 310. This course provides students with a generalized background in the interdisciplinary field of City, County, and Regional Land Use Planning and Zoning. Through lectures, readings, guest speakers, projects, viewing a Planning Commission and Zoning Board meeting, and class discussions, students will develop an understanding of and respect for the various ways scholars study and conceptualize comprehensive approaches and applications of urban planning experiences throughout urban, suburban, and rural environments. As Urban Studies draws from many fields, the course will explore a variety of scholarly perspectives, including history, sociology, political science, and urban studies curricula. Additionally, this course will encourage and strengthen critical thinking, analytical, practical skills in relation to these topics so that students are able to make meaningful interdisciplinary connections within both academic and public, private, and a variety of non-profit career paths in non-academic settings. Minimum Qualifications An M.A. in a relevant field Teaching and/or practical planning experience in the public or private sectors. Preferred Qualifications Professional experience in urban, suburban, and rural settings that informs pedagogy and practical experience in the field of local government Urban Planning. AICP Certification preferred. Application Materials Letter of application, including contact information for two references, and current CV. About the Program The College of Charleston’s Urban Studies major in HSS has three concentrations: Urban Planning and Administration, Urban Policy and Social Programs, and Sustainable Urbanism. The minor in Urban Studies also draws from similar HSS departments/programs and coursework related to the the concentrations, including history, sociology, political science and other urban studies courses, along with a required experiential learning component that is a key to career path development related to urban, suburban, and rural planning, zoning, and development on a local and regional basis. Review of applications begins immediately and will continue until the position is filled. Special Instructions to Applicants Is this position Grant funded? No EEO Statement The College of Charleston is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate against any individual or group on the basis of sex, gender (including gender identity and/or expression), pregnancy, race, religion, color, national origin, age, disability, military or veteran status, sexual orientation, genetic information, and other classifications protected by applicable federal, state, and local laws. For more information, please visit eop.cofc.edu . Quicklink for Posting https://jobs.cofc.edu/postings/18743 Reference Letters Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Chronicle of Higher Education CofC - Alumni Career Services College of Charleston Website Diverse: Issues in Higher Education Glassdoor Handshake HigherEdJobs Indeed.com Internal Job Posting jbcjobs (Joint Base Charleston Military & Family Readiness) Job Fair LinkedIn Monster.com Personal Referral Post and Courier Public Job Posting SC Works (SC Department of Employment and Workforce) Twitter Word of mouth Other National Labor Exchange CareerBuilder SpouseWorks Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Application Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Resume Email: jobs@cofc.edu General Information: 843.953.5512 Mailing Address: 66 George St. Charleston, SC 29424 HR Office 160 Calhoun St. Lightsey Building B36 Charleston, SC 29424 Campus Maps ©2020 All Rights Reserved. Privacy Policy To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
