    "https://jobs.cofc.edu/postings/18758": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructor of Supply Chain Management",
      "description": "College of Charleston Employment Site | Adjunct Instructor of Supply Chain Management Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Applicant Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Academic Jobs Student Jobs Contact Us Adjunct Instructor of Supply Chain Management Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Formal applications for the position must be submitted through the College’s PeopleAdmin™ site at http://jobs.cofc.edu . Submit online (1) a letter of application, (2) a recent CV, (3) unofficial graduate transcripts (official transcripts will be required for hiring), (4) a one-page statement of your teaching philosophy, (5) names and contact information of three references, and (6) optional teaching evaluations if available. The department will begin considering applications when an adjunct opportunity becomes available and will continue considering applicants until the position is filled. Questions concerning the position should be addressed to Dr. Chen-Huei Chou, Professor and Chair, at chouc@cofc.edu. Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Posting Details General Information Rank Adjunct Instructor FLSA Exempt Position Type Adjunct Internal Title Adjunct Instructor of Supply Chain Management Department Supply Chain and Information Management School/Area School of Business Posting Number A2026038P Specialty and subspecialty, if any, sought Courses to be covered DSCI 232 Business Statistics (3 credit hours) DSCI 304 Production and Operations Management (3 credit hours) SCIM 233 Purchasing and Supply Chain Management (3 credit hours) SCIM 366 Lean and Six Sigma (3 credit hours) SCIM 373 Supply Chain Planning and Analysis (3 credit hours) SCIM 424 Supply Chain and Operations Strategy (3 credit hours) TRAN 311 Intermodal Transportation (3 credit hours) TRAN 312 Global Logistics (3 credit hours) TRAN 431 Issues in Global Logistics (3 credit hours) TRAN 432 Global Logistics Systems Management (3 credit hours) Position Description The Department of Supply Chain and Information Management at the College of Charleston seeks an Adjunct Instructor of Supply Chain Management to teach undergraduate Supply Chain Management related courses, assess student learning, maintain accurate course records, hold appropriate office hours, and communicate effectively with students and department leadership. The successful candidate will demonstrate subject-matter expertise, a commitment to student-centered teaching, and the ability to use appropriate instructional technologies. Minimum requirements include a master’s degree in Supply Chain Management, Operations Management, Industrial Engineering, or a closely related business discipline from an AACSB‑accredited business school. Prior college-level teaching experience and professional experience in Supply Chain Management or Operations Management are highly valued. Special Instructions to Applicants Formal applications for the position must be submitted through the College’s PeopleAdmin™ site at http://jobs.cofc.edu . Submit online (1) a letter of application, (2) a recent CV, (3) unofficial graduate transcripts (official transcripts will be required for hiring), (4) a one-page statement of your teaching philosophy, (5) names and contact information of three references, and (6) optional teaching evaluations if available. The department will begin considering applications when an adjunct opportunity becomes available and will continue considering applicants until the position is filled. Questions concerning the position should be addressed to Dr. Chen-Huei Chou, Professor and Chair, at chouc@cofc.edu. Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Is this position Grant funded? No EEO Statement The College of Charleston is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate against any individual or group on the basis of sex, gender (including gender identity and/or expression), pregnancy, race, religion, color, national origin, age, disability, military or veteran status, sexual orientation, genetic information, and other classifications protected by applicable federal, state, and local laws. For more information, please visit eop.cofc.edu . Quicklink for Posting https://jobs.cofc.edu/postings/18730 Reference Letters Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Chronicle of Higher Education CofC - Alumni Career Services College of Charleston Website Diverse: Issues in Higher Education Glassdoor Handshake HigherEdJobs Indeed.com Internal Job Posting jbcjobs (Joint Base Charleston Military & Family Readiness) Job Fair LinkedIn Monster.com Personal Referral Post and Courier Public Job Posting SC Works (SC Department of Employment and Workforce) Twitter Word of mouth Other National Labor Exchange CareerBuilder SpouseWorks Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Application Curriculum Vitae Teaching Philosophy Unofficial Graduate Transcripts Reference List Optional Documents Resume Unofficial Undergraduate Transcripts Student Course-Instructor Reviews Teaching Portfolio Syllabi Email: jobs@cofc.edu General Information: 843.953.5512 Mailing Address: 66 George St. Charleston, SC 29424 HR Office 160 Calhoun St. Lightsey Building B36 Charleston, SC 29424 Campus Maps ©2020 All Rights Reserved. Privacy Policy To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
