    "https://jobs.cofc.edu/postings/18757": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructor of Professional Studies",
      "description": "College of Charleston Employment Site | Adjunct Instructor of Professional Studies Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Applicant Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Academic Jobs Student Jobs Contact Us Adjunct Instructor of Professional Studies Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Formal applications for the position must be submitted through the College’s PeopleAdmin™ site at http://jobs.cofc.edu . Submit online (1) a letter of application, (2) a recent resume or CV, (3) unofficial graduate transcripts (official transcripts will be required for hiring), (4) names and contact information for three references. This position will remain open and applicants will be reviewed regularly to meet department needs. Please contact the department with questions at bps@charleston.edu . Posting Details General Information Rank Adjunct Instructor FLSA Exempt Position Type Adjunct Internal Title Adjunct Instructor of Professional Studies Department Continuing and Professional Education School/Area School of Business Posting Number A2026040P Specialty and subspecialty, if any, sought Professional Studies seeks applicants in the following subspecialty areas: Advanced Manufacturing Applied Communications Construction Management Healthcare and Medical Services Management Organizational Management Project Management Quality & Risk Management Courses to be covered Position Description The Department of Professional Studies in the School of Business at the College of Charleston invites applications for an Adjunct Instructor. The successful candidate will teach undergraduate courses in one of our seven sub-specialties, including advanced manufacturing, applied communications, construction management, healthcare and medical services management, organizational management and development, project management, and quality and risk management, or closely related fields. All courses within this program are taught in an accelerated 7-week remote format, either asynchronous online or synchronous online. This posting is not for a specific assignment or for a full-time FTE faculty position, but rather for a pool of candidates who may be considered for teaching 1-2 classes in the fall, spring, or summer sessions. QUALIFICATIONS : The minimum academic requirement is a master’s degree and course-related professional experience. Candidates should demonstrate relevant academic and/or professional expertise and a commitment to high-quality teaching. Preference will be given to candidates who are enthusiastic, collegial, engaged with students, good communicators, and team players. ABOUT THE PROGRAM : The Bachelor of Professional Studies program is the College’s primary online degree-completion program. It is intentionally designed to meet the needs of working adults who require an application-based curriculum with the flexibility of online and evening classes. The program is housed in the AACSB -accredited School of Business. Founded in 1770, the College of Charleston is a public comprehensive university committed to developing ethically centered, intellectually versatile, and globally fluent citizens who create innovative solutions to social, economic, and environmental challenges. In its 2020 edition, U.S. News & World Report ranks the College as the No. 5 top public college in the South, the No. 3 ranked college for veterans among Southern institutions, the No. 8 most innovative school in the region, the No. 8 best college for undergraduate teaching in the South, and a best value regional college. Special Instructions to Applicants Formal applications for the position must be submitted through the College’s PeopleAdmin™ site at http://jobs.cofc.edu . Submit online (1) a letter of application, (2) a recent resume or CV, (3) unofficial graduate transcripts (official transcripts will be required for hiring), (4) names and contact information for three references. This position will remain open and applicants will be reviewed regularly to meet department needs. Please contact the department with questions at bps@charleston.edu . Is this position Grant funded? No EEO Statement The College of Charleston is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate against any individual or group on the basis of sex, gender (including gender identity and/or expression), pregnancy, race, religion, color, national origin, age, disability, military or veteran status, sexual orientation, genetic information, and other classifications protected by applicable federal, state, and local laws. For more information, please visit eop.cofc.edu . Quicklink for Posting https://jobs.cofc.edu/postings/18733 Reference Letters Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Chronicle of Higher Education CofC - Alumni Career Services College of Charleston Website Diverse: Issues in Higher Education Glassdoor Handshake HigherEdJobs Indeed.com Internal Job Posting jbcjobs (Joint Base Charleston Military & Family Readiness) Job Fair LinkedIn Monster.com Personal Referral Post and Courier Public Job Posting SC Works (SC Department of Employment and Workforce) Twitter Word of mouth Other National Labor Exchange CareerBuilder SpouseWorks Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter / Letter of Application Unofficial Graduate Transcripts Optional Documents Curriculum Vitae Unofficial Undergraduate Transcripts Email: jobs@cofc.edu General Information: 843.953.5512 Mailing Address: 66 George St. Charleston, SC 29424 HR Office 160 Calhoun St. Lightsey Building B36 Charleston, SC 29424 Campus Maps ©2020 All Rights Reserved. Privacy Policy To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.cofc.edu/postings/18792": {
      "title": "Chair and Associate or Full Professor of French, Francophone, and Italian Studies",
      "description": "College of Charleston Employment Site | Chair and Associate or Full Professor of French, Francophone, and Italian Studies Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Applicant Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Academic Jobs Student Jobs Contact Us Chair and Associate or Full Professor of French, Francophone, and Italian Studies Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details POSTING INFORMATION Internal Title Chair and Associate or Full Professor of French, Francophone, and Italian Studies Position Type Tenured Administrative School/Area School of Languages, Cultures, and World Affairs Department French, Francophone, and Italian St Position Description The College of Charleston seeks a dynamic scholar, teacher, and academic leader at the rank of associate or full professor to serve as Chair of the Department of French, Francophone, and Italian Studies. The successful candidate will bring a strategic vision for the department, strong communication and leadership skills, and a demonstrated commitment to fostering a participatory and supportive environment. The chair will lead efforts in curricular innovation, faculty development, student success, and the continued enhancement of the department’s national reputation. The chair will hold a full-time, tenured faculty appointment in the Department of French, Francophone, and Italian Studies within the School of Languages, Cultures, and World Affairs. Candidates should have expertise in French, Francophone, or Italian Studies, or a closely related field, along with a distinguished record of research, publication, and teaching sufficient for appointment with tenure at the rank of associate or full professor. The position offers a competitive salary and a teaching load commensurate with administrative responsibilities. French, Francophone, and Italian Studies is a dynamic and vibrant department that enrolls approximately 1,000 students per semester and offers majors in French and Francophone Studies and French Teacher Education, as well as minors in French and Italian Studies. Many students combine this program with majors such as International Business, Hospitality and Tourism Management, Marketing, and International Studies. The department offers students a range of enrichment opportunities, including study abroad programs, experiential learning, student clubs, and residence in the historic French House. Please submit a cover letter, a CV, and contact information for three references by November 16, 2026. The successful candidate will demonstrate a record of academic leadership and program development as well as collegiality, professionalism, and the ability to work collaboratively with faculty, staff, and students. For more information, contact Dr. Aimee Arias, Dean, School of Languages, Cultures, and World Affairs, College of Charleston, 11 Glebe St., Charleston, SC 29424. ariasak@cofc.edu . Applicants are encouraged to visit the department website https://charleston.edu/french-italian-studies/ . To learn more about the College of Charleston, please visit www.charleston.edu . Special Instructions to Applicants Posting Date 09/21/2026 Closing Date 11/16/2026 Open Until Filled? No Posting Number F2026009P EEO Statement The College of Charleston is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate against any individual or group on the basis of sex, gender (including gender identity and/or expression), pregnancy, race, religion, color, national origin, age, disability, military or veteran status, sexual orientation, genetic information, and other classifications protected by applicable federal, state, and local laws. For more information, please visit eop.cofc.edu . Quicklink for Posting https://jobs.cofc.edu/postings/18463 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Application Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Teaching Philosophy Research and Professional Development Statement Unofficial Graduate Transcripts Other Document Teaching Portfolio Email: jobs@cofc.edu General Information: 843.953.5512 Mailing Address: 66 George St. Charleston, SC 29424 HR Office 160 Calhoun St. Lightsey Building B36 Charleston, SC 29424 Campus Maps ©2020 All Rights Reserved. Privacy Policy To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.cofc.edu/postings/18789": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructor of Nursing Education",
      "description": "College of Charleston Employment Site | Adjunct Instructor of Nursing Education Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Applicant Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Academic Jobs Student Jobs Contact Us Adjunct Instructor of Nursing Education Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Posting Details General Information Rank Adjunct Instructor FLSA Exempt Position Type Adjunct Internal Title Adjunct Instructor of Nursing Education Department Nursing Education School/Area School of Health Sciences Posting Number A2026028P Specialty and subspecialty, if any, sought RN to BSN Nursing education with previous online experience. Courses to be covered Varies Position Description The Online Nursing Faculty (Adjunct) is responsible for teaching baccalaureate-level nursing courses within the fully online RN-to- BSN program. The faculty member uses the university’s Learning Management System ( LMS ) to deliver high-quality course content, actively facilitate asynchronous discussions, evaluate student performance, and provide timely, constructive feedback. Reporting directly to the Director of Nursing Education, the adjunct faculty member serves as an educator and mentor for working registered nurses advancing their education and leadership skills. As part of their teaching responsibilities, the faculty member participates in accreditation activities and collaborates with department leadership to ensure curriculum integrity, student retention, and compliance with national nursing education standards in the courses they teach. Special Instructions to Applicants Is this position Grant funded? No EEO Statement The College of Charleston is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate against any individual or group on the basis of sex, gender (including gender identity and/or expression), pregnancy, race, religion, color, national origin, age, disability, military or veteran status, sexual orientation, genetic information, and other classifications protected by applicable federal, state, and local laws. For more information, please visit eop.cofc.edu . Quicklink for Posting https://jobs.cofc.edu/postings/18621 Reference Letters Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Chronicle of Higher Education CofC - Alumni Career Services College of Charleston Website Diverse: Issues in Higher Education Glassdoor Handshake HigherEdJobs Indeed.com Internal Job Posting jbcjobs (Joint Base Charleston Military & Family Readiness) Job Fair LinkedIn Monster.com Personal Referral Post and Courier Public Job Posting SC Works (SC Department of Employment and Workforce) Twitter Word of mouth Other National Labor Exchange CareerBuilder SpouseWorks Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Unofficial Graduate Transcripts Optional Documents Resume Cover Letter / Letter of Application Teaching Philosophy Unofficial Undergraduate Transcripts Reference List Email: jobs@cofc.edu General Information: 843.953.5512 Mailing Address: 66 George St. Charleston, SC 29424 HR Office 160 Calhoun St. Lightsey Building B36 Charleston, SC 29424 Campus Maps ©2020 All Rights Reserved. Privacy Policy To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.cofc.edu/postings/18803": {
      "title": "Associate/Full Professor and Academic Program Director of Biomedical Engineering",
      "description": "College of Charleston Employment Site | Associate/Full Professor and Academic Program Director of Biomedical Engineering Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Applicant Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Academic Jobs Student Jobs Contact Us Associate/Full Professor and Academic Program Director of Biomedical Engineering Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Review of applications will begin on 12/01/2026 and will continue until the position is filled. Posting Details POSTING INFORMATION Internal Title Associate/Full Professor and Academic Program Director of Biomedical Engineering Position Type Tenure-track School/Area School of Engineering, Computer Science, and Mathematics Department Engineering Position Description The School of Engineering, Computing, and Mathematics ( SECM ) at the College of Charleston invites applications for a tenure-track or tenured faculty position to serve as the founding Academic Program Director of Biomedical Engineering at the rank of Associate Professor or Professor, with an anticipated start date of August 2027. Appointment rank, tenure status, and salary will be commensurate with the candidate’s qualifications and experience. Teaching and research are mutually supportive activities at the College of Charleston. The successful applicant will have a plan for bringing a research program to the College. Relevant areas include biomedical device design, biomechanics, biomaterials, medical imaging, rehabilitation engineering, neural engineering, bioinstrumentation, computational biomedicine, or other relevant biomedical engineering topics. The successful candidate will provide academic leadership in the development, implementation, and continuous improvement of a new Bachelor of Science (B.S.) program in Biomedical Engineering. This position presents a unique opportunity for an entrepreneurial educator and scholar to lead the creation of a distinctive biomedical engineering program at a rapidly growing public university located in one of the nation’s most vibrant medical and technology corridors. This is an exciting time to join the University as it continues strong enrollment growth and is strategically investing to increase national prominence. The Program Director will work collaboratively with engineering faculty, faculty in the School of Health Sciences and School of Natural and Environmental Sciences, administrators across the College, and external stakeholders to develop and launch the Biomedical Engineering program. The successful candidate will lead efforts to establish program educational objectives, student outcomes, curriculum, laboratories, assessment processes, industry partnerships, and an advisory board necessary to support future accreditation by the Engineering Accreditation Commission ( EAC ) of ABET . Established in 2023 as part of this new School, the Department of Engineering currently offers Bachelor of Science degrees in Electrical Engineering and Systems Engineering, Integrated Engineering and Business, and a Bachelor of Arts in General Engineering. The department is continuing its strategic expansion by the addition of both Biomedical Engineering and Mechanical Engineering programs. The addition of Biomedical Engineering represents a major strategic initiative for the College and aligns with opportunities for expanding collaboration with the nearby Medical University of South Carolina ( MUSC ), regional healthcare providers, and South Carolina’s growing biomedical and medical device industries. SECM offers a friendly, dynamic, and collaborative environment, with ample opportunities for interdisciplinary partnerships across the university’s ten schools. The university is located just blocks from the Medical University of South Carolina ( MUSC ), providing exceptional opportunities for collaboration in biomedical research, healthcare innovation, and student experiential learning. Appointment as Academic Program Director is expected upon hire and is accompanied by teaching load reassignment to support program leadership and administrative responsibilities. The Program Director appointment is a renewable administrative assignment reporting to the Department Chair of Engineering. Major Responsibilities · Provide leadership in the establishment, growth, and continuous improvement of the Biomedical Engineering B.S. program. · Lead curriculum development and implementation consistent with institutional and ABET accreditation requirements. · Mentor and provide professional development for junior faculty in Biomedical Engineering. · Develop and maintain program educational objectives, student outcomes, assessment processes, and continuous improvement plans. · Lead and coordinate preparation for initial and continuing ABET accreditation. · Coordinate course scheduling, enrollment planning, and instructional staffing for the Biomedical Engineering program. · Recruit, advise, and mentor Biomedical Engineering students. · Collaborate with Engineering Department leadership regarding faculty hiring needs, resource planning, and laboratory development. · Develop partnerships with MUSC , healthcare systems, medical device companies, and other external stakeholders. · Establish and maintain an effective Industrial Advisory Board. · Prepare annual reports, strategic plans, and budget requests for the program. · Promote student success through experiential learning, undergraduate research, internships, and industry engagement. · Maintain an active program of scholarship and participate in service activities consistent with faculty rank and expectations. · Teach undergraduate engineering courses. Required Qualifications · Ph.D. or equivalent terminal degree in Biomedical Engineering or a closely related engineering discipline. · Proven track record of teaching, advising, and mentoring students. · Evidence of excellence in academic research and scholarly achievement appropriate for appointment at the rank sought. · Academic qualifications sufficient to teach core biomedical engineering coursework, including human physiology. · Experience with engineering curriculum development. · Knowledge of ABET accreditation processes and requirements. · Strong written, organizational, and interpersonal communication skills. · Demonstrated ability to work collaboratively across disciplines and academic units. Additional Qualifications by Rank · Associate Professor: Record of teaching effectiveness, scholarly achievement, and service consistent with appointment at the associate professor level. The ability to be granted tenure at time of hire preferred. · Professor: Distinguished record of teaching, scholarship, and leadership sufficient for appointment with tenure at the professor rank. Preferred Qualifications · Experience developing, coordinating, or directing an academic program. · Experience with ABET self-study preparation, accreditation reviews, or continuous improvement processes. · Experience in biomedical device design, biomechanics, biomaterials, medical imaging, rehabilitation engineering, neural engineering, bioinstrumentation, computational biomedicine, or related areas. · Experience developing biomedical engineering teaching and research laboratories. · Experience collaborating with healthcare organizations, medical schools, or industry partners. · Experience securing externally funded research, educational, or workforce development programs. · Interdisciplinary experience spanning engineering and health-related fields. · Possessing an ABET accredited B.S. Degree in Biomedical Engineering · Experience or familiarity with Pre-med advising · Post-doctoral and/or industry experience · Experience with regulatory processes (e.g. FDA ) · Professional Engineer (PE) licensure Application Instructions Qualified candidates should submit: · Letter of application addressing qualifications for the position and interest in developing a new Biomedical Engineering program. · Curriculum vitae. · Statement of teaching philosophy. · Statement of research and scholarly interests. · Statement describing experience with program development, accreditation, academic leadership, or related activities. · Names and contact information for three references. For additional information, contact: Dr. Wes Hitt Chair, Biomedical Engineering Program Director Search Committee Department of Engineering School of Engineering, Computing, and Mathematics College of Charleston 66 George Street Charleston, SC 29424 Email: hittw@cofc.edu About the College of Charleston and the School of Engineering, Computing, and Mathematics: Founded in 1770, the College of Charleston is a comprehensive public university and committed to developing intellectually versatile and globally fluent citizens who create innovative solutions to social, economic, and technological challenges. A primarily undergraduate institution with strong graduate degree programs, the university prides itself on excellence in education. The university enrolls over 10,000 undergraduate and 1000 graduate students. In its 2025 edition, U.S. News & World Report ranks the College as the No. 4 top public university in the south, the No. 5 ranked college for veterans among southern institutions, the No. 9 most innovative school in the region, and the No. 3 best college for undergraduate teaching in the south and a best value regional college. The College is in the heart of beautiful Charleston. Visit the College’s website at https://www.cofc.edu . Visit the School’s website at https://charleston.edu/school-engineering-computing-mathematics/ . Special Instructions to Applicants Review of applications will begin on 12/01/2026 and will continue until the position is filled. Posting Date 10/30/2026 Closing Date Open Until Filled? No Posting Number F2026024P EEO Statement The College of Charleston is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate against any individual or group on the basis of sex, gender (including gender identity and/or expression), pregnancy, race, religion, color, national origin, age, disability, military or veteran status, sexual orientation, genetic information, and other classifications protected by applicable federal, state, and local laws. For more information, please visit eop.cofc.edu . Quicklink for Posting https://jobs.cofc.edu/postings/18761 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Chronicle of Higher Education CofC - Alumni Career Services College of Charleston Website Diverse: Issues in Higher Education Glassdoor Handshake HigherEdJobs Indeed.com Internal Job Posting jbcjobs (Joint Base Charleston Military & Family Readiness) Job Fair LinkedIn Monster.com Personal Referral Post and Courier Public Job Posting SC Works (SC Department of Employment and Workforce) Twitter Word of mouth Other National Labor Exchange CareerBuilder SpouseWorks Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Application Curriculum Vitae Teaching Philosophy Research and Professional Development Statement Reference List Statement of Leadership Philosophy Optional Documents Resume Form DD 214 Email: jobs@cofc.edu General Information: 843.953.5512 Mailing Address: 66 George St. Charleston, SC 29424 HR Office 160 Calhoun St. Lightsey Building B36 Charleston, SC 29424 Campus Maps ©2020 All Rights Reserved. Privacy Policy To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
